pport #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Support Bridgewater State University Giving Day by making a donation to help provide transformative opportunities and resources for every student. Schedule an appointment with a career advisor on Handshake by clicking on this image. Complete our report a job or internship form to share your success story with other students and alumni. Upcoming Events September Sep 09 Event: Explore Deloitte: Real Talk & Real Work Panel Wed, Sep 9 from 4pm - 4:30pm Wednesday, September 9th from 4pm - 4:30pm Sep 09 Event: TD Securities Information Session: 2027 Global Transaction Banking Summer Program Wed, Sep 9 from 5:30pm - 6pm Wednesday, September 9th from 5:30pm - 6pm Sep 10 Event: Resume-Mania Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Navigating the Career Fair Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Rising Builder Series: Avatar and Identity ⭐ Thu, Sep 10 from 6pm - 7pm Thursday, September 10th from 6pm - 7pm Sep 14 Event: Citizens Property and Procurement: All You Need to Know for Recruiting Season Mon, Sep 14 from 1pm - 1:30pm Monday, September 14th from 1pm - 1:30pm Sep 15 Event: Dress for Success Tue, Sep 15 from 11am - 3pm Tuesday, September 15th from 11am - 3pm Sep 15 Event: Merck Manufacturing Leadership Development Program (MLDP) Info Session Tue, Sep 15 from 12pm - 1pm Tuesday, September 15th from 12pm - 1pm Sep 15 Event: Explore Deloitte: Kickstart Your Job Search Tue, Sep 15 from 1pm - 1:30pm Tuesday, September 15th from 1pm - 1:30pm Sep 16 Event: Drop-In Resume Review Day for the Internship & Job Fair Wed, Sep 16 from 10am - 3pm Wednesday, September 16th from 10am - 3pm See more events Access How to Guides Latest Jobs & Internships Special Programs Report a Job or Internship Career Outcomes Career Toolkit Career Services & Internships Partners View All Design Your Life & Career Career Services & Internships Office will help you think early and often about where you want to go while at BSU and in your future career and life. Students and alumni can meet 1:1 with a career & internship advisor for help with the following topics: • Major Exploration • Career and Life Design Advising • Resume & Cover Letter • Internship Search • Job Search • LinkedIn and Networking • Interview Basics • Practice Interview • Graduate School Planning • Specialty Internship Programs Featured Articles One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Share This: Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on Facebook Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey and you don’t have to travel it alone. At Bridgewater State University, first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students have access to dedicated support through the Career Services & Internships office, including career advising,  … By Katie Vagen Show author info Katie Vagen Director of Career Development Send Email Read more » Finding the Right Major for You Share This: Share Finding the Right Major for You on Facebook Share Finding the Right Major for You on LinkedIn Share Finding the Right Major for You on X Copy Link If you’re still deciding on a major or wanting to make a change, you’re not alone. According to a the National Academic Advising Association (NACADA) “up to 75% of college students change their major at least once” during their educational  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist Share This: Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on Facebook Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on LinkedIn Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on X Copy Link The shift from campus life to a full-time corporate role requires more than just showing up on day one. This guide breaks down the practical steps recent graduates need to take in late summer to set themselves up for success,  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Share This: Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on Facebook Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on LinkedIn Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on X Copy Link By Vicki Salemi, career expert at Monster.com Congrats, you crushed your summer internship! If you clicked with your colleagues and boss, enjoyed the work, and felt right at home with company culture, you may be disappointed that the internship is  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? Share This: Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on Facebook Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on LinkedIn Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on X Copy Link A staffing firm acts as a bridge between employers and job seekers. Companies rely on staffing agencies to find qualified employees quickly, while job seekers gain access to opportunities that may not be advertised publicly. Many staffing firms recruit for  … By Gerald Tang Show author info Gerald Tang Executive Director Send Email Read more » View All Blogs Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Job & Internship Opportunities Political Canvasser North Shore Strategies Hudson Institute Political Studies Summer Fellowship in Theory and Practice of Politics Hudson Institute Business Development Executive Metric Search Manufacturing Technical Writer (6 months) Quest Global Account Manager Integrated Services Data Axle See All Jobs Quick Links Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More CareerSpring Share This: Share CareerSpring on Facebook Share CareerSpring on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. We provide a one-of-a-kind … Read More View All Resources Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
