    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/customize-your-experience-with-careers-bridgew-edu/": {
      "title": "Customize Your Experience with Careers.Bridgew.Edu",
      "description": "Customize Your Experience with Careers.Bridgew.Edu – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Customize Your Experience with Careers.Bridgew.Edu Log In – Career Services & Internship Program | Bridgewater State University To get started, click on the “Log in” link above (or at the top right corner of the page) and log in or “Sign up” to create an account. Current students can access the site through single sign-on. Alumni, Faculty, Staff and Employers will need to sign up for an account.  Once you enter and confirm your email address, setup a password and enter in your graduation date or anticipated graduation date. Users will then be asked to setup their alerts for email notifications.  These will be customized emails sent just to you based on your preferences on the next page. The next page is the Preferences page. This is where you can customize your content; your selections will inform what type of content is sent to you in your individualized newsletter. You can choose blog topics, types of opportunities that interest you, events and industries of interest, etc. You can choose as few or as many communities and interest areas as you wish. Once you have made your selections, click the “Next” button located on the lower right-hand corner of the page. Next you can set the frequency at which you will receive newsletters. After you have made your selections, click the “Finish” button and you are done. You can revise your preferences at any time by following this process. At the upper right area of the main page, you will see a drop-down menu “Welcome, First Name”; click on it and it will provide your profile navigation options. Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
    },
    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/student/": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Students",
      "description": "Undergraduate Students – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Undergraduate Students Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Are you a BSU student looking for comprehensive career development support? Look no further than the Career Services & Internships Office! From your first day of classes to beyond graduation, the office offers one-on-one and group sessions on resume writing, cover letter writing, interview preparation, internship search strategies, job search strategies, how to network, and career exploration and assessment. Plus, the online portal Handshake connects you directly with employers for jobs and internships. Throughout the year, the office hosts industry-specific panels, networking events, and career fairs for you to meet with potential employers. With a variety of internship and professional development programs, the Career Services & Internships Office ensures you are career-ready for the workforce. Below is a sample list of career development activities. Be sure to work with a career advisor to devise your own plan. First Year Students Take Focus 2, a self-paced, online career assessment tool to learn more about yourself and explore careers. Review What can I do with this major ? to learn more about majors and career options. Activate your Handshake account and update your profile. Schedule an appointment via Handshake with a career advisor to discuss majors and career directions. Attend career events, fairs, and workshops to learn more about the internship search process and to network with prospective employers. Sophomore Update your Handshake account. Schedule an appointment with a career advisor via Handshake to construct your resume and cover letter. Explore and apply for micro-internships via Parker Dewey. Search for career opportunities through Handshake. Participate in employer information sessions, career workshops, and events. Attend the fall and spring Job & Internship Fairs, the STEM Career Expo, and the Industry Insiders event series. Learn more about the for-credit internship process and funding options. Junior Year Update your Handshake account. Refine your resume and apply for internships via Handshake and other job search websites. Attend workshops, industry insider events, Bear Trek visits and career fairs to network with employers. Secure an internship and complete the application for a credited internship before the add/drop deadline. Consider participating in the Career Services & Internships Office Signature Programs such as The Washington Center, Semester in the City, MGH Aspire, and Virtual Internships. Learn more and apply for funding to support your internship. Schedule an appointment with a career advisor via Handshake to develop your own job search plan. Senior Year and Beyond Schedule an appointment with a career advisor via Handshake to develop your own job search plan. Explore or apply for graduate school, fellowships, or gap year programs. Update your Handshake account and include your personal email account on your profile to ensure continuous access. Participate in for-credit internships; apply for funding when appropriate. Attend workshops, industry insider events, Bear Trek visits, and career fairs to network with employers. Take part in the Job Search Boot Camp series. We encourage everyone to review the Rights and Responsibilities for Job Seekers, Employers, and Career Centers put forth by NACE as we uphold these standards at BSU. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Share This: Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on Facebook Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey and you don’t have to travel it alone. At Bridgewater State University, first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students have access to dedicated support through the Career Services & Internships office, including career advising,  … By Katie Vagen Show author info Katie Vagen Director of Career Development Send Email Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 50 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Upcoming Events September Sep 09 Event: Explore Deloitte: Real Talk & Real Work Panel Wed, Sep 9 from 4pm - 4:30pm Wednesday, September 9th from 4pm - 4:30pm Sep 09 Event: TD Securities Information Session: 2027 Global Transaction Banking Summer Program Wed, Sep 9 from 5:30pm - 6pm Wednesday, September 9th from 5:30pm - 6pm Sep 10 Event: Navigating the Career Fair Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Resume-Mania Thu