    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/transfer-students/": {
      "title": "Transfer Students",
      "description": "Transfer Students – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Transfer Students Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Welcome to Bridgewater State University! At BSU, we understand that transfer students have unique needs when it comes to career development. Whether you’re transitioning from another college or university or planning to transfer to a four-year institution, the Career Services & Internships office is here to support and empower you as you navigate your academic journey and prepare for your future career. Here’s what we offer: Career Advising : Our experienced career advisors provide personalized guidance to all students whether you’re decided on a major and career path or not. We help you explore career paths that align with your interests and strengths, set goals, and design your next steps for career and life. Career Assessments : Take advantage of our various career assessments that reveal your values, interests, personality, and skills. We’ll help you interpret the results and connect them to potential career paths. Resume Critiques and Mock Interviews : Craft a compelling resume and practice interview techniques to boost your confidence and marketability. Internship Programs and Funding: Apply to special internship programs such as the Washington Center or Semester in the City.  Get access to thousands of other internship postings via Handshake. Remember, you can apply for internship funding for unpaid opportunities. Job Search Strategy : Learn effective job search strategies, including how to tailor your applications and stand out to employers. Networking & LinkedIn: Develop a stand-out LinkedIn profile and learn how to search for BSU alumni and other professionals to network with. Graduate School: Explore graduate school options, fellowships, and research opportunities. We are here to help you unpack the graduate school application process. Workshops, Events, and Career Fairs: Learn new skills and connect with employers for jobs and internships. And more! Check out all of our current events and programs on Handshake . Questions about academics or how your credits will transfer in or out? Contact our colleagues in BSU’s Transfer Services . We look forward to supporting you throughout your time at BSU. Go Bears! Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Finding the Right Major for You Share This: Share Finding the Right Major for You on Facebook Share Finding the Right Major for You on LinkedIn Share Finding the Right Major for You on X Copy Link If you’re still deciding on a major or wanting to make a change, you’re not alone. According to a the National Academic Advising Association (NACADA) “up to 75% of college students change their major at least once” during their educational  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia