    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/staff/": {
      "title": "Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Faculty & Staff Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Let’s collaborate: Together we can make #BSUWorks. The Career Services & Internships Office welcomes the opportunity to collaborate with faculty and staff in a variety of ways to help students and alumni meet their career goals. We encourage all faculty and staff to review the NACE Guide to Ethical and Legal Standards in Student Hiring to have the latest information on best practices and standards in the field. Please review the opportunities below or contact our office at: 508-531-1328 or careerservices@bridgew.edu. Handshake Access for Faculty and Staff, Our Career Management System for BSU Students and Alum ni Handshake: BSU’s online recruiting system where employers post jobs and internships, career events, register for job fairs and interact with students. Faculty can learn about current job openings, internship opportunities, employer events, job fairs, and career-related resources available to their students. All faculty and staff have a student account created for them which you can access with Single Sign-On at the Handshake Login Page .  If off campus or choosing to use the Handshake mobile app (available in Google and Apple stores), your username is your full BSU email address and the corresponding password.  If you have any questions or trouble logging-in, please feel free to call the office at: 508-531-1328.  ​​​​​​​​​​​ Faculty & Staff Toolkit: Embed Career Development Into Your Curriculum This Faculty & Staff Career Toolkit is designed to equip faculty and staff with user-friendly resources to help integrate career development resources and strategies into classroom instruction, advising sessions, and student support programming. With easy access to career content, reflection prompts, skill-building activities, and up-to-date industry insights, this hub supports you in preparing students for the ever-changing world of work—without overhauling your course or schedule. Career Services & Internships Workshop Presentation – Don’t Cancel That Class! Interested in having Career Services & Internships present an interactive workshop for your class, organizations, residence hall, program, or event?  A brief description of each of the workshops is listed below.  We are now presenting in-person or virtual workshops. Please complete and submit a Workshop Request Form to schedule a workshop for your group. Workshops are 50 minutes in length. Please allow two weeks advance notice when selecting your program date A minimum of 10 participants is requested Workshops may be scheduled Monday – Thursday 9:00 AM – 6:00 PM Available Presentation Topics Choosing a Major – Learn about yourself and how to research a major and careers. Cover Letter – Learn how write an effective cover letter that showcases your skills and talents to an employer. Effective Interviewing – Are you ready to sell yourself in an interview? Learn about the interviewing process, commonly asked questions, and tips to help you interview with confidence. Graduate School Planning – Learn how to research schools and navigate the admissions process including test preparation, writing your essay, and more. How to Work a Job Fair – Learn the tips and tricks of navigating a career fair. Informational Interviewing and LinkedIn – Learn how to network through informational interviews with alumni and professionals in your career field. Internships – Learn how students can participate in internships while at BSU.  Credit, funding, and the internship search process will be discussed. Intro to Career Services & Internships Office – Learn about Career Services & Internships resources, programs, events, and other student supports. Job Search – Learn how to organize your job search including networking, job search engines, and the tools needed for a successful search. Resume Writing – Learn how to sell your experience and qualifications to potential employers. Learn resume guidelines to help jump start your career. Encourage Students to Setup an Appointment with a Career Advisor Our office meets with students on all the topics below. Students can schedule a meeting by either calling our office at: 508-531-1328 or schedule online on Handshake . Appointment Topics/Meeting Types Intro to Career Services and Internships – The advisor will provide a broad overview of our resources including appointment types, events, programs, and online tools such as FOCUS, Handshake, and What Can I Do With This Major? Choosing A Major – The advisor will help the student conduct self-assessment, explore majors and careers, and narrow down their options for choosing a major. Career Counseling – The advisor will help the student understand what career options are available to them based on their major as well as their values, interests, personality, and skills using a variety of tools and resources. Resume/Cover Letter – The advisor will critique the student’s draft of a resume or cover letter for content, formatting, spelling, and grammar while teaching the student to align the resume or cover letter to industry standards. Internship Advising – The advisor will discuss the internship process at BSU, how to search for an internship, set a realistic timeline, outline action steps, and highlight online resources including internship search sites. Funding opportunities and academic credit will also be discussed. International Internships – The advisor will discuss how to research organizations that offer international internship experiences by placing students in an internship abroad, or in major cities across the U.S., during the summer. The Washington Center Program – Spend a semester in Washington, DC!  During this appointment, we will explain the options available, talk through the application process, and discuss how to fund the experience. Semester in the City Program – Gain experience through an internship in Boston where you can make a difference in the world and earn a full semester of college credit while building skills to solve humanity’s toughest challenges. Learn more about eligibility for the program, the application process, and how to fund the experience. Networking – The advisor will discuss how to develop and maintain a professional network using a variety of methods including LinkedIn and informational interviewing. LinkedIn Profile Review – The advisor will review the student’s LinkedIn profile for content and help them understand all of the options for adding information and experiences to complete their profile. Effective Interviewing – The advisor will talk about the do’s and don’ts of interviewing, employer expectations, professional dress, commonly asked questions, and follow-up. Practice Interview – The advisor will conduct a “real” interview and offer feedback. The student is required to submit an internship or job description of interest and a resume to the advisor in advance. Interview attire can be critiqued as well but is not required.  *It is recommended that the students complete an Effective Interviewing appointment prior to a mock interview if possible.* Job Search – The advisor will discuss how to organize a job search, set a realistic timeline, outline action steps, and highlight online resources including job search sites. Grad School Advising – The advisor will discuss the graduate school timeline, application process, and how to search for graduate programs. Share and Use Top Career Resources in the Classroom and in Advising Below are some of the top tools available on our website to help students explore career options, find opportunities and prepare for interviews. FOCUS 2 Online Career Assessment Explore your career interest, values, personality, and skills through this self-paced, online career guidance tool. Create an account or login as a returning user by visiting the FOCUS 2 Login page. Enter the Access Code as Bridgew . Schedule an appointment with a Career Counselor if you would like to discuss your Focus 2 results. What Can I Do With This Major Website What Can I Do With This Major? – Learn about typical career paths and types of employers that hire people with each major, as well as strategies to make you a more marketable candidate. Labor Market Insights This tool, located throughout our website, allows you to research all major career paths to gain information on the field, salary, job outlook, top employers, skills in demand and more. You can find this information for nationwide data or search for any state data as well. Utilize the Labor Market Insights tool on this page to check out this resource and all the valuable information you can find on it. Connect With BSU Alumni on LinkedIn LinkedIn Alumni Tool – Talk to BSU alumni to learn about career paths of interest. Check out the LinkedIn & Informational Interviewing Guide for sample LinkedIn messages as well as sample questions that you may want to ask if you schedule an informational interview with a BSU alum. Big Interview: Virtual Practice Interview Software Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. There are hundreds of interview sets and questions covering a variety of industry and interview types. The system uses AI technology to track your eye contact, rate of speech and a variety of other factors to help you improve your skill set. As you complete interview sets, you can track your improvement and progress. Current BSU students can log-in to Big Interview through Single Sign-On . BSU alumni can create an account on the Big Interview homepage using registration code “5600”. Special thanks to Enterprise Mobility for this product available for BSU students and alumni. Encourage Students to Gain Experience There are a variety of ways that students can gain experience on campus through research, volunteerism, study abroad and more.  Our office shares resources with students on gaining internship experience in a variety of ways from semester based credited internships, virtual internships, micro-internships and projects, semesters in DC and more!  Check out our Internship Resources , Signature Internship Programs as well as Internship Funding information pages to be up-to-date on all the options available to your students! They can also setup an appointment to meet with a career advisor to discuss their search process. Classroom Visits At the start of the fall and spring semesters, Career Services & Internships Office staff make brief 5 minute visits at the start of classes to talk about the services, programs and events we have for the upcoming semester.  Be sure your students know all the important resources we can provide them for career success.  Interested faculty can email Laurent Troland at: ltroland@bridgew.edu to be added to our list for next semester. Bring You and Your Students to a Career Fair or Event Each year our office hosts a variety of career fairs, industry insiders events, workshops, site visit and panel programs. Check out our current listing of fairs and events on our website as well as on Handshake’s events page . Career Outcomes Survey Each year the Career Services & Internships Office conducts a first destination survey of recent graduates 6 months after graduation to learn more about their post-BSU plans including employment, continuing education and more. Check out our Career Outcomes page for full details. Roundtable Meeting with Career Services & Internships Staff Throughout the academic year, our office looks to setup meetings with faculty and staff from different departments to learn more about what is happening in your area: new trends, new programs, new staff and more!  If interested in setting up a time to collaborate, contact Katie Vagen at: kvagen@bridgew.edu Collaborative University Business Experiences (CUBEs) The CUBEs initiative brings together a team of faculty to explore ways to reinforce career readiness through curriculum. CUBEs projects will help students better prepare for their future careers. Although CUBEs collaboration focuses on capstone/research projects embedded in BSU’s course design, we also welcome other opportunities to collaborate with employers, such as guest speakers, facility tours, networking events, job shadowing, and internships. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Finding the Right Major for You Share This: Share Finding the Right Major for You on Facebook Share Finding the Right Major for You on LinkedIn Share Finding the Right Major for You on X Copy Link If you’re still deciding on a major or wanting to make a change, you’re not alone. According to a the National Academic Advising Association (NACADA) “up to 75% of college students change their major at least once” during their educational  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 50 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Upcoming Events September Sep 09 Event: Explore Deloitte: Real Talk & Real Work Panel Wed, Sep 9 from 4pm - 4:30pm Wednesday, September 9th from 4pm - 4:30pm Sep 09 Event: TD Securities Information Session: 2027 Global Transaction Banking Summer Program Wed, Sep 9 from 5:30pm - 6pm Wednesday, September 9th from 5:30pm - 6pm Sep 10 Event: Navigating the Career Fair Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Resume-Mania Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Rising Builder Series: Avatar and Identity ⭐ Thu, Sep 10 from 6pm - 7pm Thursday, September 10th from 6pm - 7pm View More Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More CareerSpring Share This: Share CareerSpring on Facebook Share CareerSpring on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. We provide a one-of-a-kind … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Finding the Right Major for You Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Faculty Are Key to Student Career Success View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
