    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/parents-families/": {
      "title": "Parents & Families",
      "description": "Parents & Families – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Parents & Families Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos The Career Services & Internships Office provides comprehensive career development support for all BSU students and alumni. Whether your student is considering a career in the arts, education, science, business, government, nonprofit, or technology sectors, our professional advisors are here to help them explore and plan for their career pursuits. Supporting students’ career development is crucial for their future success. As parents and family members, you play a vital role in guiding and encouraging them. We encourage you to review the Rights and Responsibilities for Job Seekers, Employers, and Career Centers put forth by NACE as we uphold these standards at BSU. Meanwhile, here are some practical steps you can take: Encourage Career Exploration: As the world of work continues to evolve, there are many career options and career pathways. We recommend that students utilize their college years to explore various career options through participation of experiential learning opportunities such as internships, research, class projects, service learning, on or off-campus employment, and campus programs. Parents and family members can encourage students to engage in these experiences to develop career skills and competencies and gain further insight into themselves and the choices before them. Acquire World of Work Knowledge: Help your students learn about different professions and industries. Discuss various career paths, job roles, and workplace dynamics. Exposure to real-world scenarios can broaden their perspective. Refer your students to Handshake to explore jobs and internships and participate in career development events and programs. Our career advisors are here to help your students to design their own career development journey, so don’t hesitate to encourage them to schedule an appointment with us through Handshake. Participate in Career Programs and Trainings : Our office offers a variety of resources and program offerings for students.  Skill-building workshops on topics such as resume writing, interviewing, job search strategies, using LinkedIn, networking, and applying to graduate school are also offered throughout the year. Students receive regular communications from us, so remind them to stay informed about career resources, workshops, and training opportunities, along with opportunities to attend career fairs, industry panels, and networking events. We also encourage parents and families to share job or internship leads available at your organization and encourage your employer to explore recruitment partnerships with us. Remember, your support and guidance can significantly impact your student’s career journey. By actively participating and fostering a positive environment, you contribute to their growth and success. We look forward to working with you and your student. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Finding the Right Major for You Share This: Share Finding the Right Major for You on Facebook Share Finding the Right Major for You on LinkedIn Share Finding the Right Major for You on X Copy Link If you’re still deciding on a major or wanting to make a change, you’re not alone. According to a the National Academic Advising Association (NACADA) “up to 75% of college students change their major at least once” during their educational  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 50 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Upcoming Events September Sep 09 Event: Explore Deloitte: Real Talk & Real Work Panel Wed, Sep 9 from 4pm - 4:30pm Wednesday, September 9th from 4pm - 4:30pm Sep 09 Event: TD Securities Information Session: 2027 Global Transaction Banking Summer Program Wed, Sep 9 from 5:30pm - 6pm Wednesday, September 9th from 5:30pm - 6pm Sep 10 Event: Navigating the Career Fair Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Resume-Mania Thu, Sep 10 from 1pm - 3pm Thursday, September 10th from 1pm - 3pm Sep 10 Event: Rising Builder Series: Avatar and Identity ⭐ Thu, Sep 10 from 6pm - 7pm Thursday, September 10th from 6pm - 7pm View More Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More CareerSpring Share This: Share CareerSpring on Facebook Share CareerSpring on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. We provide a one-of-a-kind … Read More View All Resources Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The information below will allow you to see career outcomes for the most recent graduating class that we have surveyed.  This data is a summary of key findings, but you can read the full reports on our CSI Reports website . 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination The first destination survey provides insights on what graduates are doing within 6 months of completing their degree.  Data is collected through a survey housed in our Handshake platform and sent via email and made available on our website prior to graduation and in the months afterwards. Top Employers This is a list of the most frequently reported employers where graduates are working after completing their degree.  This is not a full listing of all employers, just the most commonly reported.  For information on top internship sites for each class year, visit our CSI Reports site for the list of Student Internship Sites . Starting Salary The salary information below is based on self-reported data from graduates willing to provide salary data for their post-graduate employment.  This is base salary and does not include bonuses or other benefits. Employment Locations BSU graduates are working all over the United States, but contribute greatly to the Massachusetts economy with over 85% of graduates working in the commonwealth on average.  Additionally many other graduates work in the New England region. United States World Top Universities Below is a listing of the most common colleges/universities that BSU graduates are attending for their continued education.  This is not an exhaustive list. Degree Types The chart below displays the types of continuing education degrees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Featured Articles One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Finding the Right Major for You Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Supporting BSU Graduate Students View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 