    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/asian-pacific-islanders-native-american/": {
      "title": "Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American",
      "description": "Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for Asian, Pacific Islanders, and Native Americans At Bridgewater State University there are many support services for Asian, Pacific Islanders and Native American students who are preparing to enter the workforce. The Career Services & Internships Office has pulled together select resources and websites that can be helpful for the career development and job search process.  In addition, be sure to utilize the resources of the Lewis and Gaines Center for Inclusion and Equity here at BSU.  If you have questions or concerns about the job search process, we encourage you to schedule an appointment with one of our career advisors who will be happy to meet with you. Below are some helpful resources: America’s Best Employers For Diversity 2024 according to Forbes. Ascend is the largest, non-profit Pan-Asian membership organization for business professionals in North America, with 60,000+ senior executives, professionals, and MBA/undergraduate students. The Asian American Advertising Federation is dedicated to advancing the Asian American marketing and advertising industry for Asian American consumers through education, advocacy, and collaboration. Asian American Architects and Engineers Association is committed to providing a platform for empowering Asian American professionals working in the built environment. Asian American Journalists Association believes in promoting diversity in news coverage and in newsrooms. Asian American Hotel Owners Association is the largest hotel owner’s association in the country for Asian Americans. Asian American Professional Association inspires, develops, and promotes Asian American and minority professionals to maximize their career and leadership potential. Asian Pacific American Medical Student Association is a national organization of medical and pre-medical students committed to addressing the unique health challenges of Asian American, Native Hawaiian, & Pacific Islander (AANHPI) communities. Asian Pacific American Medical Student Association is committed to addressing the unique health challenges of Asian Pacific American communities through education, outreach, advocacy, and service. Asian Real Estate Association of America is a membership-based professional association organization for Asian American housing and real estate professionals. CareerExploration.com provides a long list of Native American Professional Associations by industry. CareerForum.net is a career site for Japanese-English bilingual job seekers. Diversity Job Board posts immediate positions available for diverse candidates. DiversityWorking.com is a diversity job search site for all ethnic and sexual orientation groups. Diversity Job-Seeker Career and Job Resources focuses on uniting diversity-driven employers with people of color, women, veterans, older workers, individuals with disabilities, and members of the LGBTQIA+ community. IMDiversity.com provides career and self-development information to individuals from diverse backgrounds, specifically African Americans, Asian Americans, Latine Americans, Native Americans, and women. JobStars USA provides a list of recommended Asian professional associations and organizations. National Asian Pacific American Bar Association is the national association of Asian Pacific American attorneys, judges, law professors, and law students. National Association of Asian American Professionals is a non-profit organization that cultivates and empowers Asian & Pacific Islander leaders. Native Peoples Recruit.com provides an online directory of resources and information for Native Americans, Alaska Natives, Native Hawaiians, and other indigenous groups of people living under the U.S. jurisdiction. PharmaDiversity Job Board focuses on matching diverse candidates with all types of jobs in the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and healthcare industries from accountants and administrators to sales to research. Society of Asian Scientists and Engineers is dedicated to advancing its members to help them achieve their full career potential. Seramount provides a list of key organizations serving the Native American community. Talent Ally offers career networks for diverse communities including the iHispano, Black, Asian, Pride, Ability, Women, and Military Networks. The Inroads Internship Program works at the college level to prepare talented, diverse students across the country for corporate readiness with business soft skills, real-world leadership development activities, academic and career support, and an opportunity for a paid internship. Velvet Jobs recommends a list of 31 career resources for Native Americans. WorkplaceDiversity.com is an online community that includes resources and tools to help students connect with employers across multiple career fields and offers a job-board for corporate recruiters who are seeking experienced diverse candidates. Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
