    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/black-african-american/": {
      "title": "Black/African American",
      "description": "Black/African American – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Black/African American Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for Black/African American Students At Bridgewater State University there are many support services for Black/African American students who are preparing to enter the workforce. The Career Services & Internship Program Office has pulled together select resources and websites that can be helpful for the career development and job search process.  In addition, be sure to utilize the resources of the Lewis & Gaines Center for Inclusion & Equity here at BSU.  If you have questions or concerns about the job search process, we encourage you to schedule an appointment with one of our career advisors who will be happy to meet with you. Job Boards America’s Best Employers For Diversity 2023 according to Forbes. Black Jobs | Careers and Employment For African Americans a website featuring the latest well-paying job opportunities for African American job seekers from companies who are sincerely dedicated to diversity hiring. Black Job Center is an inclusive job board for the Black community Black UpStart teaches aspiring Black entrepreneurs how to start a successful and profitable business through an intense, culturally-relevant popup school. Black Career Network provides access to networking, training, educational, and employment opportunities for diverse professionals. Black Career Women’s Network is a national career development organization dedicated to fostering the professional growth of Black women. BLK Capital Management BLK Capital Management Corp. is a 100% Black-owned and student-run non-profit. They promote the financial achievement of Black students through educational programming, hands-on experience, and professional mentorship. Diversity.com a female and minority owned business connecting underrepresented talent with forward-thinking employers committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. DiversityinHigherEducation niche job board focused on diversity in higher education DiversityinEducation niche job board focused on diversity in education Diversity Job Board posts immediate positions available for diverse candidates. Diversity Jobs: African American and Black Job Seekers focuses on uniting diversity-driven employers with people of color, women, veterans, older workers, individuals with disabilities, and members of the LGBTQIA+ community. DiversityWorking.com is a diversity job search site for all ethnic and sexual orientation groups. Hack.Diversity is an access-centered organization offering substantial Fellowship opportunities in the tech industry.  With sites in Boston and NYC, student participants focus on professional skills development, technical team projects, and industry exposure. HIREBLACKNOW founded by Black women with recruiting backgrounds, #HIREBLACK has an innovative approach to identify, attract, and connect high-performing diverse talent with companies and organizations. IMDiversity.com – a hub of information and resources regarding graduate/professional schools, industry reports and studies, diversity issues and extracurricular activities. Initially established exclusively for diverse populations but now available to all.  The site includes a job board full of career opportunities mainly for experienced/professional-level job seekers. National Society of Black Engineers Job Board NSBE supports and promotes the aspirations of collegiate and pre-collegiate students and technical professionals in engineering and technology. National Urban League Jobs Network connects Black students and young working professionals looking for career opportunities with employers nationwide. Nemnet Diversity Recruitment helps recruit and retain diverse teachers, administrators, and coaches. Newsweek Magazine publishes an annual list of America’s Greatest Workplaces for Black Americans . PharmaDiversity Job Board focuses on matching diverse candidates with all types of jobs in the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and healthcare industries from accountants and administrators to sales to research. POCIT a job board for people of color working in the tech industry. SEO Careers SEO Careers prepares high achieving Black, Latinx, and Native American undergraduates for summer internships across Wall Street, commercial real estate, technology and corporate America, creating a more equitable society by closing the career opportunity gap for motivated young people. TalentAlly / Black Career Network: Empowering Black Professionals : a career-building ecosystem designed to help candidates stand out and inclusive employers find the right talent, offering specialized affinity sites (Black, Hispanic, Asian, Pride, Ability, Women, and Military) The National Council of Negro Women, Inc. leads, empowers, and advocates for women of African descent, and their families and communities. The Inroads Internship Program works at the college level to prepare talented, diverse students across the country for corporate readiness with business soft skills, real-world leadership development activities, academic and career support, and an opportunity for a paid internship. WorkplaceDiversity.com is an online community that includes resources and tools to help students connect with employers across multiple career fields and offers a job-board for corporate recruiters who are seeking experienced diverse candidates. Mentoring & Networks Mentor Me Black — Black-to-Black Personal and Professional Mentorship Platform is the first technology platform purpose-built for Black-to-Black Personal and Professional Mentorship. Free, volunteer-driven, and open to anyone seeking guidance from Black mentors. UndocuBlack Network a multi-generational network of Black immigrants that fosters community, facilitates access to resources, and advocates for a thriving future. 100 Black Men of America, Inc. recognized as one of the nation’s top African American led mentoring programs. Unfold Her Project – Empowering Black Girls & Women a community dedicated to uplifting and empowering Black girls and women through transformative mentorship, education, and skill development. Black Woman Leading® – Black Woman Leading supports Black women throughout their career life cycle as they learn, heal and grow in their leadership capacity. WELCOME | Black Girl White Coat a nonprofit organization that provides academic resources, mentorship, and scholarships to Black women pursuing careers in healthcare. ColorStack a nonprofit dedicated to increasing the number of Black and Latinx Computer Science technologists. National Black MBA Association advances underrepresented professionals by providing unparalleled access to career development, economic empowerment, and educational opportunities. Management Leadership for Tomorrow Career Prep Programs are designed to help you develop your skills, gain confidence, and discover the career pathways that fit you best. The Career Accelerator program offers personalized mentorship for first-generation, low-income students. Internships NextGen Leaders Internship Program — Blackconnect a one-semester, experiential learning opportunity that places motivated college students with Black Connect member businesses as Host Sites across a wide range of industries. Students gain real-world skills, mentorship, career exposure, and pathways to leadership — while supporting the growth of Black-owned businesses nationwide. (Open to all majors, in-person, virtual, or hybrid options) Congressional Black Caucus Foundation Internships CBCF’s internship programs prepare college students and young professionals to become principled leaders, skilled policy analysts, and informed advocates by exposing them to the processes that develop national policies and implement them – from Capitol Hill to federal field offices. Program participants receive housing, a stipend, office placements, and opportunities to meet and interact with professional legislators and leaders working in all branches of government. Black Wall Street USA Internship Program Interns in this program will develop professionally, gain a strong network, and cultivate a sense of personal empowerment and responsibility for community development. As Black Wall Street USA focuses on economic empowerment and cultural awareness, the program offers distinctive opportunities for interns to grow as future leaders, advocates, and professionals in social equity, business development, and cultural engagement. Minority Access National Internship Program designed to allow talented undergraduate and graduate students experience the diversity and scope of career opportunities available in the federal, state and local government and participating private business entities. William Randolph Hearst Endowed Fellowship – Aspen Institute Established in 1995, the William Randolph Hearst Fellowship: Encouraging Tomorrow’s Diverse Nonprofit Leaders opens students to new career pathways in the social sector, creating a pipeline from which a new generation of leadership is emerging. The AAAS Diverse Voices in Science Journalism Internship for students who are interested in pursuing a career in journalism and want to learn more about science writing. This program is designed for individuals with a deep commitment to extending the reach of science journalism into communities where there is currently limited participation. By training science journalists with a commitment to diverse communities, the program will help to build the capacity of those individuals to report on scientific issues to a general audience and expand access to the profession to persons including, but not limited to, individuals from diverse populations. NAACP Internships and Fellowships these programs not only expose students and young professionals to diverse issues and their complexities, but also provide a network of resources and practitioners for guidance. They offer the next generation of civil rights advocates and social justice activists the chance to delve into NAACP’s robust agenda. NAACP Creative Fellowship The NAACP Creative Fellowship program, in partnership with Adobe, is a 14-week paid program designed to equip emerging post-production professionals with skills in video editing, motion graphics, sound design, and social media content creation.  This next-level opportunity is open to individuals with some editing experience who are ready to launch their careers in post-production. Young Women & the Science of Beauty Experience NAACP Youth & College and L’Oréal have teamed up to create exclusive, behind-the-scenes creative industry immersion experiences for young women interested in careers in STEAM, fashion, beauty, and creative production. These one-day experiences are designed to provide real-world exposure, mentorship, and career insight by connecting participants directly with industry professionals in live and studio-based environments. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search Share This: Share Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search   on Facebook Share Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search   on LinkedIn Share Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search   on X Copy Link Many of you may have received or seen a message like this during the job search : “Thank you for your interest in (Name of Position). You were one of many impressive candidates who responded to our job posting. However, after  … By Samuel Arruda Show author info Samuel Arruda Career & Life Design Advisor Send Email Read more » BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Share This: Share BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! on Facebook Share BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! on LinkedIn Share BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! on X Copy Link We are incredibly proud of the work happening at Bridgewater State University’s Career Services & Internships Office as we continue to support students and advance the mission of Bridgewater State University as an engine for supporting the Massachusetts local and  … By Gerald Tang Show author info Gerald Tang Executive Director Send Email Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 13 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
