    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/first-generation/": {
      "title": "First-Generation",
      "description": "First-Generation – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes First-Generation Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for First-Generation Students Do you come from a family where your parents or guardians did not complete a four-year college or university degree? You are not alone. Approximately 47% of BSU students are first-generation and are navigating similar challenges and triumphs. Career Services & Internships is dedicated to supporting first-generation students in their career development. We have pulled together select resources and websites that can be helpful for the career development, networking, and job search process.  If you need help uncovering the unknowns within the career development process, we encourage you to schedule an appointment with one of our career advisors who will be happy to meet with you. CareerSpring Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. BSU has partnered with CareerSpring which provides a one-of-a-kind Career Platform to help unlock the future potential of first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students by providing career information and resources. You can explore careers, develop skills, network and get advice as well as launch your internship or job search. Visit the CareerSpring website to request access today! FirstGen Society is a national social organization dedicated specifically for first-generation college students and alumni. I’m First is a resource that supports and informs first-generation students and their families while starting and navigating college. Rise First empowers first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students and professionals nationwide to achieve their full potential by providing life and career advice, lists of support resources, and mentorship opportunities through a technology platform with online tools. The Scholarship System provides the ultimate first-generation scholarship list. America Needs You is an organization that fights for economic mobility for ambitious, first-generation college students by providing transformative mentorship and intensive career development. First Gen Summit is an annual conference hosted by First Gen Leadership; an organization that convenes, connects, and inspires first-generation students and professionals in their leadership journey. Performance Project brings together young adults ages 15-22 who self-identify as “first-generation,” for artistic training, leadership development, and inter-generational mentoring. U.S. News & World Report provides “Tips for First-Generation Students.” Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More CareerSpring Share This: Share CareerSpring on Facebook Share CareerSpring on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. We provide a one-of-a-kind … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
