    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/international/": {
      "title": "International Students",
      "description": "International Students – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes International Students Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Resources for International Students and Scholars The Career Services & Internship Program Office works closely with international students at BSU as they navigate all aspect of career development, from career exploration to preparing job search materials to understanding the job interview process. Whether you are exploring internships and job opportunities in the United States or globally, we encourage you to work closely with our career advisors throughout this process. Your Role as an International Student It is important for international students to understand their visa status, eligibility to obtain work authorizations, and the job search process. Be sure to work closely with the International Students and Scholars Services Office (ISSS) to understand the latest guidelines and regulations. Searching for a Job and Internship in the United States It is essential for international students to fully understand their eligibility to work in the United States. Keep up to date with information from the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) regarding work authorization . Unless you are working on campus, you will obtain work authorization under CPT or OPT to pursue jobs and internships off-campus. Please connect with the ISSS before accepting any positions to ensure you comply with your visa requirements. When applying for opportunities, companies may ask you the question – Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Answer as truthfully as possible. For example, if you are an international student on an F-1 visa and want to work in the United States after your OPT finishes, then the answer to this question is yes. A company who accepts OPT and/or CPT is willing to hire international students who have OPT and/or CPT. This does not necessarily mean they will provide sponsorship (H1B), and it is up to you to talk to your employer about whether they will sponsor you to stay with the organization after your OPT finishes. Benefits of Being an International Student or Scholar For many international students, applying for jobs in the United States and connecting with employers and alumni can be daunting, and it may feel very different from how you apply for jobs back home. In the US job search process, we encourage you to make connections with industry professionals and employers early and often (i.e. Networking). A great way to start is to find alumni who are from similar backgrounds. Check out the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn or attend events that are listed on Handshake . Having an instant connection through your cultural background can help ease the nerves of networking. You’ll also gain valuable tips about how they networked effectively. Consider highlighting some of these qualities you bring to a job or internship: Cultural diversity and global perspective: This gives you a perspective/mindset that may be different than domestic students. Insight into your field and specialization. Language Skills: Having fluency in multiple languages can benefit you in your work field. Adaptability: Showing employers that you can easily adapt to new cultures, which is a great skill! Demonstrated ability to overcome obstacles: This can help highlight your strengths and weaknesses. Career Resources USCIS – https://www.uscis.gov/ MyVisaJobs – Reports for H1B Visas and Visa Sponsor Profiles – http://www.myvisajobs.com/ One to World – One-to-world.org/ Office of Foreign Labor Certification; US Dept of Labor – visas, fees, policies, and regulations – https://www.dol.gov/agencies/eta/foreign-labor International Students – https://www.internationalstudent.com/ Employer Information – Glassdoor.com H1B Database – https://h1bdata.info/index.php Open Avenues Foundation website Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Should international students hide that status from employers when job hunting? Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
