    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/latinx/": {
      "title": "Latine",
      "description": "Latine – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Latine Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for Latine Students At Bridgewater State University there are many support services for Latine students who are preparing to enter the workforce. The Career Services & Internships Office has pulled together select resources and websites that can be helpful for the career development and job search process.  In addition, be sure to utilize the resources of the Lewis & Gaines Center for Inclusion & Equity here at BSU.  If you have questions or concerns about the job search process, we encourage you to schedule an appointment with one of our career advisors who will be happy to meet with you. Below are some helpful resources: Association of Latino Professionals For America offers networking and professional leadership development opportunities.  Additionally, members have access to over 50,000 paid summer internships and experienced job opportunities. Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute provides leadership, public service, and policy experiences to outstanding Latine students and young professionals.  The Institute also convenes Members of Congress and other elected officials, corporate executives, nonprofit advocates, and thought leaders to discuss issues facing the Latine community and the nation. Diversity Job Board posts immediate positions available for diverse candidates. Diversity Job-Seeker Career and Job Resources focuses on uniting diversity-driven employers with people of color, women, veterans, older workers, individuals with disabilities, and members of the LGBTQIA+ community. Diversity Employers is a print and digital publication offering a job board with career opportunities that specifically target new college graduates of diverse backgrounds in every industry nationwide. Hispanic Alliance for Career Enhancement is a national non-profit dedicated to the employment, development, and advancement of current and aspiring Hispanic professionals. Hispanic/Latino Professionals Association provides job and career information for individuals and job seekers. Hispanic Marketing Council advocates for responsible and intentional investment in Hispanic marketing. iHispano: Jobs and Careers for Latino Professionals is a job board. IMDiversity.com is dedicated to providing career and self-development information to individuals from diverse backgrounds, specifically African Americans, Asian Americans, Latine Americans, Native Americans, and women. National Association of Hispanic Journalists is an educational and charitable association dedicated to the recognition and professional advancement of Hispanic students, professionals, and educators in the field of journalism. National Association of Puerto Rican and Hispanic Social Workers is a job board and provides information on the profession to members of the Puerto Rican Hispanic community. Nemnet Diversity Recruitment helps recruit and retain diverse teachers, administrators, and coaches. PharmaDiversity Job Board focuses on matching diverse candidates with all types of jobs in the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and healthcare industries from accountants and administrators to sales to research. Saludos: Hispanic Employment Website is a job board of employers and organizations which are searching for qualified bilingual, bicultural, and minority applicants. Society for Advancement of Chicanos/Hispanic & Native Americans in Science is a resource to explore hundreds of job opportunities, career insights, and resources, as well as to connect with over 4,000 employers. Talent Ally offers career networks for diverse communities including the iHispano, Black, Asian, Pride, Ability, Women, and Military Networks. United States Hispanic Chamber of Commerce actively promotes the economic growth, development, and interests of more than 5 million Hispanic-owned businesses. WorkplaceDiversity.com is an online community that includes resources and tools to help students connect with employers across multiple career fields and offers a job-board for corporate recruiters who are seeking experienced diverse candidates. Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
