    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/lgbtqia/": {
      "title": "LGBTQIA+",
      "description": "LGBTQIA+ – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes LGBTQIA+ Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for LGBTQIA+ Students LGBTQIA+ students may have unique career planning and job search questions and considerations.  The Career Services & Internships Office has identified select resources and websites that you may find helpful in your career planning process and job search.  Our career advisors are all Safe Zone allies and are happy to meet with you, providing a safe space to support your career development and job search success. In addition, be sure to utilize the resources of the GLBTA Pride Center here at BSU. Researching Employers and Your Rights The American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) provides individuals assistance if they have been discriminated against. America’s Best Employers For Diversity according to Forbes. Coming Out at Work is a resource, produced by The Human Rights Campaign (HRC), that assists one in the decision to come out at work and how to go about doing it. GLBTQ Legal Advocates & Defenders (GLAD ) specifies what legal protections one has in the state of Massachusetts. Human Rights Campaign Foundation’s Corporate Equality Index is the national benchmarking tool on corporate policies, practices, and benefits pertinent to lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, and queer employees. Indeed.com provides an excellent article and video on finding LGBTQ+ friendly employers and provides job search advice. Out & Equal is the premier global nonprofit organization working exclusively on LGBTQ+ workplace equality. Through worldwide programs, strategic corporate partnerships, and sought-after events, Out & Equal helps LGBTQ+ individuals realize their fullest, most authentic potential, while supporting organizations in creating cultures of belonging for all. Job/Internship Sites for the LGBTQIA+ Community Diversity Employers is a print and digital publicationoffering a job board with career opportunities that specifically target new college graduates of diverse backgrounds in every industry nationwide. DiversityWorking.com is a diversity job search site for all ethnic and sexual orientation groups. Idealist.org is a top nonprofit/human services job search site that has a dedicated LGBTQ issue area filter. LGBTQ Career Network is a job board for LGBTQ community. LGBTConnect is a job board connecting employers with the LGBT community. Nemnet Diversity Recruitment helps recruit and retain diverse Teachers, Administrators, and Coaches. PharmaDiversity Job Board focuses on matching diverse candidates with all types of jobs in the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and healthcare industries from accountants and administrators to sales to research. Out and Equal is a job board for LGBTQ community. WorkplaceDiversity.com is an online community that includes resources and tools to help students connect with employers across multiple career fields and offers a job-board for corporate recruiters who are seeking experienced diverse candidates. Networking and Community Groups LGBTQ Professional and Student Associations is a list, produced by The Human Rights (HRC), of LGBTQ+ Professional and Student Associations, broken down by industry. LinkedIn is a great networking tool. Join networking groups that are in the LGBTQ+ Community such as Out & Equal’s LGBTQ+ CareerLink Network . Just search LGBTQ in groups. National LGBT Chamber of Commerce is the largest advocacy organization dedicated to expanding economic opportunities and advancements for LGBTQ people, and the exclusive certifying body for LGBTQ-owned businesses. Out 4 Undergrad invites a diverse class of high-achieving LGBTQ2+ students to unique conferences, where they’re inspired to pursue ambitious careers. Out Professionals is the leading nonprofit networking organization for LGBTQ (Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, and Queer/Questioning) professionals in the USA. Out In Tech is the world’s largest non-profit community of LGBTQ+ tech leaders. Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
