    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/veterans/": {
      "title": "Veterans",
      "description": "Veterans – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Veterans Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Career Resources for Veterans Career Services & Internships supports BSU students who are currently serving in the military, as well as veterans, by providing guidance on career planning, major selection, and the transition from student to civilian or military careers. We have compiled a selection of resources and websites to assist with career development and the job search process. We also encourage you to take advantage of the services offered by Military and Veteran Student Services at BSU. If you have questions about your career goals or the job search process, schedule an appointment with one of our career advisors. They are available to provide personalized guidance and support. Careers in the Military provides thousands of career options within the military. My Next Move for Veterans offers career resources for veterans including the O*Net OnLine’s Military Crosswalk Search that provides descriptions of military jobs by title and military occupation code.​​​​​​​ The Military Skills Translator matches military experience to civilian jobs. The CareerOneStop Veteran and Military Transition Center is a one-stop website for employment, training, and financial help after military service. Veterans’ Employment and Career Transition Advisor provides important employment information and resources in your state, including contact information for your local Director for Veterans’ Employment and Training, as well as state government jobs. The National Resource Directory is a database of validated resources that supports recovery, rehabilitation, and reintegration for service members, veterans, family members, and caregivers. American Corporate Partners (ACP) is a national nonprofit organization focused on helping returning Veterans and Active-Duty Spouses find their next careers through one-on-one mentoring, networking and online career advice. FourBlock is a nation-wide community of veterans and employers dedicated to transforming the veteran transition process. 50strong is a national, collaborative, industry-led effort supporting hundreds of employers and thousands of military-affiliated jobseekers. Military Friendly Employers is a list of employers that meet Military Friendly standards that measure an organization’s commitment, effort, and success in creating sustainable and meaningful benefits for the military community. Candorful | Nail That Interview connects transitioning military service members and career transitioners with experienced interview coaches for live personal practice job interviews so they can nail that interview. The Student Veterans of America is the premier organization leading service, research, programs, and advocacy for veterans in higher education. RecruitMilitary is a comprehensive military-to-civilian recruiting company that connects military veterans, transitioning military service members, and their spouses with employment opportunities. The Paralyzed Veterans of America’s Veterans Career Program , formerly known as PAVE, provides FREE employment support and vocational counseling assistance to ALL veterans, transitioning service members, spouses, and caregivers. The U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) Pathways Internship Program allows students to join the VA in career positions that emphasize long term development and training. Hiring Our Heroes works to connect the military community with meaningful employment opportunities. USAJOBS connects job seekers with federal employment opportunities across the United States and around the world. If you’re a veteran who served on active duty in the U.S. Armed Forces and were separated under honorable conditions, you may be eligible for veterans’ preference, as well as other veteran specific hiring options. MilitaryHire connects veterans of America’s armed forces, military spouses, and immediate family members with employers who value their experience and skills. FedsHireVets – OPM.gov provides details about the federal hiring process and the career resources and opportunities available to veterans, transitioning service members, and military family members. DiversityWorking provides job listings for veterans that are tailored specifically to match the unique skills and experiences. G.I. Jobs will help you navigate your postmilitary career. Hire Veterans offers the very best and relevant career opportunities offered by world class veteran friendly companies who want YOU! Corporate Gray connects those who have served in the military with employers nationwide via military-focused job fairs and through their website. Veterans Employment Services is the go-to site for veterans or service members looking for their first civilian job after the military, wanting a career change, or hoping to start their own business. Veteran Jobs Mission represents more than 315 companies on a mission to keep veterans, current service members, and their spouses a part of their long-term talent strategies. ClearanceJobs is the largest career network for professionals with federal government security clearance. HigherEd Military can assist you in identifying and landing your dream job in higher education. The American Council on Education (ACE) Military Guide will assist you with interpreting occupations you have held in the military as well as describe courses you attended. The U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs provides you with career and employer assistance. DiscoverVA provides a listing of VA approved resources outside the Department. This does not include VA-accredited Veteran Service Organizations (VSO). Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Career Resources Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More What Can I Do With This Major? Share This: Share What Can I Do With This Major? on Facebook Share What Can I Do With This Major? on LinkedIn Share What Can I Do With This Major? on X Copy Link Learn about career options based on your studies at BSU. The website provide you with information regarding career options and … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles Ice Cold Responses: Rejection and Silence During Your Job Search BSU Works – Class of 2025 graduates are going places! Considering Health-related Graduate Programs? Considering Law School? Resume Writing: Tips and Tricks for Your Career Service Resource Library View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
