    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/aviation/": {
      "title": "Aviation",
      "description": "Aviation – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Aviation Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Careers in Aviation The aviation industry incorporates all business directly involved with air travel and transportation by airplane, helicopter, and unmanned aircraft, such as drones. The key players of the aviation industry are aircraft manufacturers, airlines, airports, regulatory bodies, and aircraft maintenance, repair, and overhaul (MRO). The aviation industry is crucial for global commerce and travel, connecting goods and people across continents, countries, and cultures. What Can I Do With an Aviation Career? There are a variety of career options available to those in the Aviation industry.  Focus areas in Aviation include: Aerospace Engineering Career Overview Air Traffic Control Career Overview Aircraft Maintenance Career Overview Aviation Management Career Overview Aviation Safety Career Overview Cabin Crew Career Overview Civil Career Overview and Military Aviation Career Overview Pilot Career Overview Flight Instruction Career Overview Aviation Transport/Logistics Career Overview Gaining Experience in Aviation The Aviation Science program at Bridgewater State University includes comprehensive FAA approved training via simulators and BSU’s fleet of aircraft. Full details are available on the BSU Aviation Department’s Flight Training page. . Students also gain experience through internships with various airlines, airports and municipalities in addition to airline partnership programs: Listing of Aviation Science Internships and Experiences. Resources for Aviation Careers Professional Associations Professional Pilots Association (PPA) Aircraft Owners Pilots Association (AOPA) National Business Aviation Association (NBAA) Women in Aviation International (WAI) Organization of Black Aerospace Professionals (OBAP) National Gay Pilots Association (NGPA) Employers That Work With BSU Cape Air Endeavor Air Flexjet Mike Gouilan Aviation Republic Airways Transportation Security Administration (TSA) Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Air Traffic Controllers Practice Interview Airline Pilots, Co-Pilots and Flight Engineers Practice Interview Airfield Operations Specialists Practice Interview Aviation Inspectors Practice Interview Commercial Pilots Practice Interview Flight Attendants/Cabin Crew Practice Interview Aviation Job Boards All Airlines in the United States List : Most major carriers and regional airlines post directly on their website and some on larger jobs boards such as Indeed and LinkedIn. Research airlines of interest and bookmark their careers/human resources pages. AviaNation Worldwide Jobs Site Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) Aviation Careers MassPort Jobs National Business Aviation Association Jobs Board National Gay Pilots Association Jobs Board BSU Clubs and Organizations Alpha Eta Rho – Alpha Eta Rho is a professional co-ed aviation fraternity. Civil Air Patrol Senior Squadron – Established in 1941, Civil Air Patrol (CAP) is the volunteer civilian auxiliary of the United States Air Force. Women in Aviation – Women in Aviation was created with the goal to introduce this remarkable career path for students who are curious to learn more. Networking and LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Having trouble breaking into the field? Want advice from professionals? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network page ” for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a huge resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find aviation professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Still have questions? Setup an appointment on Handshake with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Job & Internship Opportunities Junior Network Operation Center Technician Software Galaxy Systems Airfield Safety Officer San Francisco International Airport Electronic Warfare Engineer DCS Corp Senior Maintenance Technician - Third Shift Allegis Global Solutions Lateral Police Officer The Blue Line Electronics Technician Amphenol CIT See All Jobs Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The information below will allow you to see career outcomes for the most recent graduating class that we have surveyed.  This data is a summary of key findings, but you can read the full reports on our CSI Reports website . 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination The first destination survey provides insights on what graduates are doing within 6 months of completing their degree.  Data is collected through a survey housed in our Handshake platform and sent via email and made available on our website prior to graduation and in the months afterwards. Top Employers This is a list of the most frequently reported employers where graduates are working after completing their degree.  This is not a full listing of all employers, just the most commonly reported.  For information on top internship sites for each class year, visit our CSI Reports site for the list of Student Internship Sites . Starting Salary The salary information below is based on self-reported data from graduates willing to provide salary data for their post-graduate employment.  This is base salary and does not include bonuses or other benefits. Employment Locations BSU graduates are working all over the United States, but contribute greatly to the Massachusetts economy with over 85% of graduates working in the commonwealth on average.  Additionally many other graduates work in the New England region. United States World Top Universities Below is a listing of the most common colleges/universities that BSU graduates are attending for their continued education.  This is not an exhaustive list. Degree Types The chart below displays the types of continuing education degrees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Career Resources Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on X Copy Link Every year, the Career Services & Internship Program Office invites our employer partners to conduct corporate presentations on campus and … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake o