      "description": "Communications, Marketing and Media – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Communications, Marketing and Media Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Careers in Communications, Marketing, and Media The communications, marketing, and media industry incorporates all organizations and professionals involved in the creation, management, distribution, and promotion of messages and content across digital, print, broadcast, and experiential platforms. Key players in this industry include advertising and marketing agencies, media and publishing companies, film and television studios, news organizations, public relations firms, digital and social media platforms, and in-house communication teams across corporate, nonprofit, and government sectors. This industry plays a vital role in shaping public perception, culture, and consumer behavior by informing, entertaining, and connecting audiences across communities, industries, and global markets. What Can I Do With a Career in Communications, Marketing, and Media? There are a variety of career options available to those in the Communications, Marketing, and Media industry. Focus areas in Communications, Marketing, and Media include: Advertising Career Overview Athletics and Sport Career Overview Business Studies Career Overview Cinema Studies Career Overview Communication Studies Career Overview Electronic Media / Broadcasting Career Overview Hotel, Restaurant, and Tourism Career Overview Journalism Career Overview Marketing Career Overview Music Business Career Overview Public Relations Career Overview Gaining Experience in Communications, Marketing, and Media Build real-world experience through a variety of hands-on learning opportunities that complement classroom learning. Internships & Micro-Internships Internships allow you to apply in-classroom learning in professional settings while building skills, confidence, and career clarity. BSU students have gained experience with television and radio stations, nonprofits, media outlets, government offices, and more. You can also participate in paid micro-internships through Parker Dewey Micro-Internship Program, completing short-term, professional projects without a long-term commitment. Clubs and Organizations Communication, marketing, and media focused clubs give you opportunities to build portfolios, collaborate with peers, and connect with professionals. Student-run clubs & organizations offer hands-on leadership, creative, and professional development experiences. Students can hold leadership positions within these organizations such as president, vice president, event planner, or social media coordinator allowing you to gain valuable management, communication, and additional skills to strengthen your resume. Study Abroad Students are encouraged to expand their global perspective through short-term travel courses and semester or year long BSU study abroad programs . Resources for Communication, Marketing and Media Careers Professional Associations American Marketing Association American Society of Cinematographers American Cinema Editors Association of Talent Agents Broadcast Education Association Business Marketing Association Direct Marketing Association Public Relations Society of America Employers That Work With BSU Ametek Brookfield Brown University DraftKings FAMILY Movement Inc. JPMorganChase Light Foundation Massachusetts State Senate NCAA New York Film Academy Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Art & Design Practice Interview Advertising Practice Interview Marketing Practice Interview Public Relations Practice Interview TV, Film, & Radio Practice Interview Communications, Marketing, and Media Job Boards Ad Age Careers Ad Week Jobs Advertising Crossings Creativepool Creativehotlist EntertainmentCareers.net Film and Television Production Directory / Employment Opportunities iHireMarketing Journalism Jobs MedioBistro PRSA Jobcenter: Public Relations Jobs PR Crossing PR News Job Board ProductionHub ShowBizJobs BSU Clubs and Organizations 91.5 WBIM-FM American Marketing Association Filmmakers Society Program Council Public Relations Student Society of America The Comment Networking and LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Having trouble breaking into the field? Want advice from professionals? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network page ” for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a huge resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find communications, marketing, and media professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Still have questions? Setup an appointment on Handshake with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Job & Internship Opportunities Political Canvasser North Shore Strategies Hudson Institute Political Studies Summer Fellowship in Theory and Practice of Politics Hudson Institute Business Development Executive Metric Search Manufacturing Technical Writer (6 months) Quest Global Account Manager Integrated Services Data Axle Director Of Sales Trilogy Health Services, LLC See All Jobs Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The information below will allow you to see career outcomes for the most recent graduating class that we have surveyed.  This data is a summary of key findings, but you can read the full reports on our CSI Reports website . 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination The first destination survey provides insights on what graduates are doing within 6 months of completing their degree.  Data is collected through a survey housed in our Handshake platform and sent via email and made available on our website prior to graduation and in the months afterwards. Top Employers This is a list of the most frequently reported employers where graduates are working after completing their degree.  This is not a full listing of all employers, just the most commonly reported.  For information on top internship sites for each class year, visit our CSI Reports site for the list of Student Internship Sites . Starting Salary The salary information below is based on self-reported data from graduates willing to provide salary data for their post-graduate employment.  This is base salary and does not include bonuses or other benefits. Employment Locations BSU graduates are working all over the United States, but contribute greatly to the Massachusetts economy with over 85% of graduates working in the commonwealth on average.  Additionally many other graduates work in the New England region. United States World Top Universities Below is a listing of the most common colleges/universities that BSU graduates are attending for their continued education.  This is not an exhaustive list. Degree Types The chart below displays the types of continuing education degrees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Career Resources Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Compan