ees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Career Resources Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on X Copy Link Every year, the Career Services & Internship Program Office invites our employer partners to conduct corporate presentations on campus and … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State Uni