    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/healthcare-wellness/": {
      "title": "Health Care and Wellness",
      "description": "Health Care and Wellness – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Health Care and Wellness Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Careers in Health Care and Wellness Health Care and Wellness careers focus on the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and management of physical and mental health across clinical, community, and organizational settings. This industry includes roles in patient care, public health, health informatics, behavioral health, rehabilitation services, healthcare administration, health education, biotechnology, and wellness promotion. There are opportunities available to students in majors including, but not limited to, exercise physiology, health science, health studies, public health, physical education, psychology, social work, sociology, biology, chemistry, and communication sciences and disorders. What Can I Do With a Career in Health Care and Wellness? There are a variety of career options available to those in the Health Care and Wellness industry. Focus areas may include: Direct Patient Care including: Physician Career Overview Physician Assistant Career Overview Nurse Career Overview Physical Therapist Career Overview Occupational Therapist Career Overview Athletic Trainer Career Overview Speech-Language Pathologist Career Overview Dietitian Career Overview Respiratory Therapist Career Overview Patient Representative Career Overview Behavioral & Mental Health including: Psychologist Career Overview Mental Health Counselor Career Overview Social Worker Career Overview Substance Abuse Counselor Career Overview Marriage and Family Therapist Career Overview Public Health & Community Wellness including: Health Educator Career Overview Epidemiologist Career Overview Community Health Worker Career Overview Environmental Health Specialist Career Overview Occupational Health and Safety Specialist Career Overview Health Technology, Data & Informatics including: Health Informatics Specialist Career Overview Bioinformatics Scientist Career Overview Clinical Data Analyst Career Overview Healthcare Administration & Management including: Health Services Manager Career Overview Compliance Officer Career Overview Research, Science & Diagnostics including: Clinical Research Coordinator Career Overview Biomedical Engineer Career Overview Medical Laboratory Scientist Career Overview Biostatistician Career Overview Wellness, Fitness & Integrative Health including: Fitness and Wellness Coordinator Career Overview Exercise Physiologist Career Overview Exercise Trainers and Fitness Instructors Career Overview Gaining Experience in Health Care and Wellness Bridgewater State University has several options for exploring careers, developing skills and experiencing health care and wellness professions.   They include: Taking introductory or elective courses in areas of interest including Exercise Physiology, Health Studies and Physical Education majors or minors , Biology including the Biomedical and Pre-medicine concentration, Health Sciences including their individual concentrations , Communications and Disorders , and Data Analytics , Social Work major and Social Welfare minor , Sociology major and minors , and the Psychology major and minor . Participate in the campus community including applying to become a Peer Educator , volunteering through BSU’s Martin Richard Institute for Social Justice, or joining the Biology, Biochemistry or Premedical Clubs,  and the PreHealth Club. Take a deeper dive into information and opportunity through BSU’s Health Careers Guide and if interested in any of the careers listed on that site, schedule an appointment with Dr. Alexandra Zilz, the pre-health advisor. Gaining practical experience through internships, including the Health Career Connections funded internship , or in your community by volunteering, participating in undergraduate research, or finding field-related part-time work in health care or wellness settings. Resources for Health Care and Wellness Careers Professional Associations American Counseling Association American Public Health Association American Psychological Association Health Information Management Systems Society National Board for Health and Wellness Coaching National Organization of Social Workers National Strength and Conditioning Association Society for Public Health Education Employers that Work with BSU Bay State Physical Therapy Boston Children’s Hospital Boston Medical Center Brockton Neighborhood Health Center High Point Treatment Center Justice Resource Institute Massachusetts Department of Children and Families MEDITECH Old Colony YMCA Southcoast Health Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Community Health Worker Practice Interview Fitness and Wellness Coordinator Practice Interview Health Educators Practice Interview Medical School Practice Interview Medical and Health Services Manager Practice Interview Medical and Clinical Laboratory Technician Practice Interview Mental Health Counselors Practice Interview Patient Representative Practice Interview Health Care and Wellness Job Boards Allied Health Jobs Cafe American Counseling Association Fitness Jobs Hospital Careers Public Health Jobs BSU Clubs & Organizations American Sign Language Club Biology Club Pre-Health Club Women in STEM Networking & LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Having trouble breaking into the field? Want advice from professionals? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network page ” for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a huge resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find aviation professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Still have questions? Setup an appointment on Handshake with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Job & Internship Opportunities Direct Support Professional Cerebral Palsy of Westchester (#R61008) Respiratory Care Assistant RHA Health Services, LLC Direct Support Staff Cooperative Production (CO-OP) AHS Medical Director - Exempt State of Vermont Registered Nurse Oneida Nation Emergency Services Dispatcher II City of Fresno See All Jobs Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North