      "title": "Public Administration, Government, and Law",
      "description": "Public Administration, Government, and Law – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Public Administration, Government, and Law Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Careers in Public Administration, Government, and Law Public administrators, government officials, and legal practitioners play a critical role in shaping the policies and systems that affect communities and societies. This work is essential to promoting effective governance, advancing equity, and addressing complex public challenges at the local, state, and federal levels. These efforts take place across a wide range of settings, including government agencies, non-profit and non-governmental organizations (NGOs), public policy and public affairs, healthcare, education, public service, and international and development organizations. Careers in these fields are diverse and interdisciplinary, encompassing roles in policy analysis, program management, advocacy, regulatory affairs, research, politics, and leadership. The strong analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills emphasized in these areas also provide a solid foundation for law and advanced legal study. What Can I Do With a Public Administration, Government, or Law Career? There are a wide variety of career options available to those pursuing Public Administration, Government, or Law. Focus areas include but are not limited to: Public Administration Public administrators implement and manage government policies and programs, overseeing public services, budgets, and operations to ensure laws and initiatives are carried out effectively and serve the public interest. Explore: Public Administration – What Can I Do With This Major Sample Roles: Administrative Services Managers , Public Relations Managers , Budget Analysts , Political Scientists/Policy Analysts , Political Scientists Government Government officials serve the public by developing, implementing, or supporting policies and programs that address community needs and uphold the laws and responsibilities of the state. Explore: Political Science and Government – What Can I Do With This Major Sample Roles: Legislators , Management Analysts , Regulatory Affairs Specialists , Compliance Officers Law Legal professionals interpret, apply, and uphold legal rules and principles to protect rights, resolve disputes, and ensure justice within society. There are many specialized practice areas. Keep in mind that a law degree opens up diverse opportunities beyond traditional legal practice. Explore: Law – What Can I Do With This Major Sample Roles: Lawyers , Judicial Law Clerks , Paralegals and Legal Assistants , Judges, Magistrate Judges, and Magistrates , Arbitrators, Mediators, and Conciliators Consider BSU’s 3+3 Law Degree: BSU/UMass Law Accelerated 3 + 3 Program | Bridgewater State University Gaining Experience in Public Administration, Government, and Law Internships, networking, and experiential learning are critical for those aspiring to a profession in these fields.  This experience can be acquired in a multitude of ways both at Bridgewater State University and beyond. Some opportunities include: BSU’s Democratic Governance & Leadership Program (DGLP) The Washington Center Academic Internship Program Federal Internships & Fellowships*: Internships/Fellowships – Careers USAJOBS Federal Internship Portal Federal Internship Finder • Go Government Future Leaders in Public Service Internship Program • Go Government Govern For America Fellowship Program *Keep in mind that federal opportunities require special documentation formatting. Check out Federal Resume tips on USAJobs.gov for more information, or book an appointment with a career advisor. State & Local Government Internship Programs Judicial Internships (local, state, or federal courts) Legal Intern or Law Clerk Internships Public Interest or Legal Aid Internships Non-Profit Internships Public Policy Internships (such as Internships | Brookings or Careers: Summer@Urban | Urban Institute ) Volunteer 3+3 program with UMass Law to earn an accelerated JD: BSU/UMass Law Accelerated 3 + 3 Program | Bridgewater State University Resources for Careers in Public Administration, Government, and Law Professional Associations American Society for Public Administration (ASPA) International City/County Management Association (ICMA) National Conference of State Legislatures (NCSL) American Political Science Association (APSA) American Bar Association (ABA) GovLoop (Young Professionals in Government / Public Service Networks) : Employers that Work with BSU Commonwealth of Massachusetts Massachusetts Trial Court Office of the Massachusetts State Treasurer and Receiver General Citizens for Citizens Town of Bridgewater New Hampshire Department of Environmental Services Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Intelligence Analyst Practice Interview Law School Practice Interview Legal Profession Practice Interview Lawyers Practice Interview Legal Support Workers, All Other Practice Interview Paralegals and Legal Assistants Practice Interview Public Relations Practice Interview Eligibility Interviewers, Government Programs Practice Interview Nonprofit Sector Practice Interview Social and Community Service Managers Practice Interview Administrative Law Judges, Adjudicators, and Hearing Officers Practice Interview Arbitrators, Mediators, and Conciliators Practice Interview Court Reporters Practice Interview Judges, Magistrate Judges, and Magistrates Practice Interview Judicial Law Clerks Practice Interview Title Examiners, Abstractors, and Searchers Practice Interview Court Clerks Practice Interview Municipal Clerks Practice Interview License Clerks Practice Interview Public Administration, Government, and Law Job Boards *Keep in mind that legislative positions often entail a decentralized job search process and may require active research and networking to explore and obtain opportunities. USA Jobs Careers in Government Devex Federal Reserve Jobs Find Law Government Jobs (by NEOGOV) Go Government GovtJobs Idealist Massachusetts Municipal Association (MMA) Career Opportunities Mass Town Careers Municipal Jobs Massachusetts Nonprofit Network Career Center Public Service Jobs Directory (PSJD) Public Affairs Council Work for Good UN Careers Individual senator and representative websites House & Senate employment bulletins BSU Clubs & Organizations Mock Trial Club The Pre-Law Society Argue This Debate Club Bipartisan Disagreement Student Government Association Martin Richard Institute for Social Justice Lewis and Gaines Center for Equity and Inclusion Networking & LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Having trouble breaking into the field? Want advice from professionals? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network page ” page for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a huge resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find aviation professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Below are a few sample groups on LinkedIn related to this industry. LinkedIn Group: Jobs in NGOs, International Development Jobs, Non Government Vacancies, Not for Profit Jobs LinkedIn Group: GovLoop LinkedIn Group: Women in Government Relations LinkedIn Group: YPFP (Young Professionals in Foreign Policy) LinkedIn Group: LAW jobs – Networking for LEGAL PROFESSIONALS – Legal jobs – Legal Careers – Lawyers – Barristers LinkedIn Group: e-LEGAL Support: Legal Secretary, Paralegals, Virtual Assistants, Law Clerks & Admin Staff Still have questions? Setup an appointment on Handshake with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Job & Internship Opportunities Substance Abuse Counselor Mary Greeley Medical Center Case Administrator U.S. District Court, Southern District of Calfornia Case Manager Global Refuge Police Officer Henrico County Police Division Investigator Surveillance Frasco, Inc. Operations Supervisor San Diego Center for Children See All Jobs Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The information below will allow you to see career outcomes for the most recent graduating class that we have surveyed.  This data is a summary of key findings, but you can read the full reports on our CSI Reports website . 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination The first destination survey provides insights on what graduates are doing within 6 months of completing their degree.  Data is collected through a survey housed in our Handshake platform and sent via email and made available on our website prior to graduation and in the months afterwards. Top Employers This is a list of the most frequently reported employers where graduates are working after completing their degree.  This is not a full listing of all employers, just the most commonly reported.  For information on top internship sites for each class year, visit our CSI Reports site for the list of Student Internship Sites . Starting Salary The salary information below is based on self-reported data from graduates willing to provide salary data for their post-graduate employment.  This is base salary and does not include bonuses or other benefits. Employment Locations BSU graduates are working all over the United States, but contribute greatly to the Massachusetts economy with over 85% of graduates working in the commonwealth on average.  Additionally many other graduates work in the New England region. United States World Top Universities Below is a listing of the most common colleges/universities that BSU graduates are attending for their continued education.  This is not an exhaustive list. Degree Types The chart below displays the types of continuing education degrees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Career Resources Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on X Copy Link Every year, the Career Services & Internship Program Office invites our employer partners to conduct corporate presentations on campus and … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting s