      "title": "STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics)",
      "description": "STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics) fields focus on innovation, problem-solving, and discovery. These careers drive advancements in healthcare, technology, infrastructure, environmental sustainability, and more. Whether you’re interested in developing new technologies, conducting research, analyzing data, or solving real-world problems, STEM offers a wide range of pathways. What Can I Do With a STEM Career? Learn about typical career paths and types of employers that hire people with each major, as well as strategies to make you a more marketable candidate. Utilize our What Can I Do With This Major? tool. Life Sciences & Health Research This field focuses on studying living systems to improve health and well-being, including biology, neuroscience, public health, among others. Professionals in this area often conduct research, work with patients or populations, and contribute to developing treatments or interventions. Sample Roles: Biologists , Neurodiagnostic Technologists , Health Informatics Specialists , Epidemiologists , Microbiologists , Geneticists , Bioinformatics Scientists Technology & Data Science This field focuses on using technology and data to solve problems, improve systems, and create innovative solutions. Professionals in this area often develop software, analyze information, manage digital systems, and use tools such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and data analytics to support organizations and communities. Sample Roles: Data Scientists , Software Developers , Information Security Analysts , Computer and Information Systems Managers , Computer and Information Research Scientists , Computer Network Architects , Information Technology Project Managers Engineering & Applied Sciences This field applies scientific and mathematical principles to design, build, and improve systems, structures, and technologies. It emphasizes problem-solving, innovation, and the practical application of knowledge to address real-world challenges. Sample Roles: Industrial Engineers , Industrial Production Managers , Mechanical Engineers , Electrical Engineers , Civil Engineers Environmental & Sustainability Careers This field centers on addressing environmental challenges and promoting sustainable practices to protect natural resources and human well-being. It involves studying ecosystems, developing solutions, and supporting policies that balance environmental and societal needs. Sample Roles: Sustainability Specialists , Industrial Ecologists , Energy Auditors , Solar Energy Systems Engineers , Environmental Engineers , Water/Wastewater Engineers , Environmental Restoration Planners Mathematics This field focuses on using quantitative reasoning, statistical analysis, and mathematical modeling to understand patterns and inform decision-making. It plays a key role in research, forecasting, and evaluating outcomes across various sectors. Sample Roles: Mathematicians , Statisticians , Data Scientists , Physicists , Financial Quantitative Analysts , Financial and Investment Analysts Gaining Experience in STEM Experience is one of the most important factors in launching a STEM career. Get Involved Early Join faculty-led research projects Participate in student organizations (STEM clubs, coding groups) Attend career fairs and networking events Build Your Resume Internships (industry or research-based) Lab or field experience Personal or class-based projects (especially for tech roles) Create a Portfolio (if applicable) GitHub (for coding projects) Research presentations or posters Data analysis projects Engage With Professional Supports Meet with Career Services & Internships team Reach out for guidance from faculty mentors Resources for STEM Careers Professional Associations Life Sciences & Health Research American Public Health Association (APHA) American Society for Microbiology (ASM) Society for Neuroscience (SfN) American Society of Human Genetics (ASHG) Technology & Data Science Association for Computing Machinery (ACM) Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) Information Systems Security Association (ISSA) Data Science Association Engineering & Applied Sciences American Society of Civil Engineers (ASCE) American Society of Mechanical Engineers (ASME) National Society of Professional Engineers (NSPE) American Institute of Chemical Engineers (AIChE) Mathematics & Quantitative Sciences American Mathematical Society (AMS) Mathematical Association of America (MAA) American Statistical Association (ASA) Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics (SIAM) Environmental & Sustainability Sciences National Association of Environmental Professionals (NAEP) Ecological Society of America (ESA) Air & Waste Management Association (A&WMA) U.S. Green Building Council (USGBC) The Ecological Society of America Employers That Work With BSU The Marine Biological Laboratory Promega Corporation Plymouth Grating Laboratory Northeastern University Single Molecule Biophysics Lab Naval Undersea Warfare Center Division Newport Coaching 4 Change Beth Israel Lahey Health KBMO Diagnostics Pace Environmental Division Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Biotech Practice Interview Chemical Engineering Practice Interview Environmental Engineering Practice Interview Biomedical Engineering Practice Interview Chemical Engineering Practice Interview Other Engineering Practice Interview A.I. Architect Practice Interview Cybersecurity Practice Interview Database Admin Practice Interview Other Technology Roles Practice Interview STEM Job Boards BioSpace Jobs Board Chemistry World Jobs Board Nature Careers Jobs Board Physics Today Jobs Board Science Careers Jobs Board Sponsored by the American Association for the Advancement of Science US Government STEM Jobs Board BSU Clubs and Organizations Biology Club Bridgewater Emission and Absorption Manipulators (BEAM) Computer Science Club Environmental Action Team Geological Society The BSU Artificial Intelligence Resource Hub (B.A.I.R Hub) Women in STEM Networking & LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Want to learn more about opportunities in the field? Want to connect with professionals in the field? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network ” page for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a great resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find STEM professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Below are a few sample groups on LinkedIn related to this industry. Life Science Networks Public Health Professionals Worldwide Data Science Central Information Systems Security Association National Society of Professional Engineers American Mathematical Society Still have questions? Setup an appointment with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Clos