      "title": "Technology and Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Technology and Cybersecurity – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Technology and Cybersecurity Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Careers in Technology and Cybersecurity The technology and cybersecurity industry encompasses a rapidly evolving profession that drives innovation, protects digital infrastructure, and shapes the way organizations operate in every field. Professionals in this space work across areas such as information systems, data analytics, software development, network administration, artificial intelligence, and cybersecurity risk management. As technology exponentially advances and cyber threats grow increasingly complex, demand continues to rise for professionals who can build, analyze, secure, and manage the online systems that we use everyday. Technology itself is the backbone of every modern industry, from healthcare and finance to education and engineering, meaning that a career in technology and cybersecurity can lead you down dozens of potential career paths in varying industries. What Can I Do With a Career in Technology and Cybersecurity? There are a variety of career options available to those in the Technology and Cybersecurity industry. Focus areas in Technology and Cybersecurity include: Artificial Intelligence Career Overview : Develop and implement a set of techniques or analytics applications to transform raw data into meaningful information using data-oriented programming languages and visualization software. Apply data mining, data modeling, natural language processing, and machine learning to extract and analyze information from large structured and unstructured datasets. Visualize, interpret, and report data findings. For more information, visit BSU’s Center for Artificial Intelligence Business Intelligence Analysis Career Overview: Produce financial and market intelligence by querying data repositories and generating periodic reports. Devise methods for identifying data patterns and trends in available information sources. Computer Networks Career Overview : Design and implement computer and information networks, such as local area networks (LAN), wide area networks (WAN), intranets, extranets, and other data communications networks. Perform network modeling, analysis, and planning, including analysis of capacity needs for network infrastructures. Cybersecurity Career Overview : Develop and oversee the implementation of information security procedures and policies. Build, maintain and upgrade security technology, such as firewalls, for the safe use of computer networks and the transmission and retrieval of information. Monitor and respond to computer security breaches, viruses, and intrusions, and perform forensic investigation. Data Services Career Overview : Administer, test, and implement computer databases, applying knowledge of database management systems. Coordinate changes to computer databases. Identify, investigate, and resolve database performance issues, database capacity, and database scalability. Digital Infrastructure Career Overview : Design strategies for enterprise databases, data warehouse systems, and multidimensional networks. Set standards for database operations, programming, query processes, and security. Model, design, and construct large relational databases or data warehouses. Create and optimize data models for warehouse infrastructure and workflow. Information Technology Support Career Overview : Analyze, test, troubleshoot, and evaluate existing network systems, such as local area networks (LAN), wide area networks (WAN), cloud networks, servers, and other data communications networks. Perform network maintenance to ensure networks operate correctly with minimal interruption. Software Development Career Overview : Research, design, update and develop computer and network software or specialized utility programs. May work with computer hardware engineers to integrate hardware and software systems, and develop specifications and performance requirements. Telecommunications Career Overview : Design or configure wired, wireless, and satellite communications systems for voice, video, and data services. Supervise installation, service, and maintenance. Web Design Career Overview : Design digital user interfaces or websites. Develop and test layouts, interfaces, functionality, and navigation menus to ensure compatibility and usability across browsers or devices. May create graphics used in websites and manage website content and links. For more info on the variety of career pathways available in the Technology and Cybersecurity industry, check out the “Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Data Science, Game Design, Information Sciences, and Management Information Systems” majors categories within What Can I Do With This Major . Gaining Experience in Technology and Cybersecurity Students can gain valuable experience in technology and cybersecurity through a variety of hands-on opportunities both on and off campus. Early on campus experiences include working in IT departments, help desks, or computer labs, by assisting faculty with computing or cybersecurity projects, or by joining tech-focused student organizations. While off campus, students can pursue internships at technology companies and government agencies or by taking on roles with local businesses and nonprofits that need support with software, technical troubleshooting, or basic security tasks. These opportunities help students understand the many career paths within information technology, cybersecurity, data, and technology services, while developing practical and critical skills that can be utilized in a wide variety of industries. Resources for Careers in Technology and Cybersecurity Professional Associations Department of Homeland Security Science & Technology National Cybersecurity Alliance National Institute of Standards and Technology SANS Employers that Work with BSU Acadia Inc. Akamai Technologies, Inc. Ames & Gough Insurance/Risk Mgm’t, Inc. Cranston Public Schools General Dynamics Granite Telecommunications MEDITECH National Right-Of-Way Land Services NETSCOUT Redwood Analysis RL Controls, LLC Sager Electronics South Shore Health Sample Practice Interview Sets on Big Interview Software Developer Practice Interview Cybersecurity Practice Interview AI Architect Practice Interview Computer Systems Analyst Practice Interview Data Analytics Practice Interview IT Specialist Practice Interview IT Support: Healthcare Practice Interview Computer Programmer Practice Interview Database Admin Practice Interview Technology and Cybersecurity Job Boards Cyber Security Jobs DICE Technology Jobs CyberJobs CyberSeek BSU Clubs & Organizations AI Olympians Student Technology Engagement Computer Science Club Networking & LinkedIn Not sure if the field is right for you? Having trouble breaking into the field? Want advice from professionals? Then it is time to network and do what we call “informational interviews” where you talk to professionals to ask for tips and advice on your career path and/or search process. View our “ Expand Your Network ” page for tips, advice, sample scripts and more to help you in this process. LinkedIn is a huge resource for following companies of interest, finding jobs and of course connecting with professionals including BSU alumni. Go to the BSU Alumni page on LinkedIn and you can search for professionals by company, industry, location and more to help you find professionals doing what you hope to do and find out how they go there! Still have questions? Set up an appointment on Handshake with a career advisor to talk about your next steps! Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Share This: Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on Facebook Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey and you don’t have to travel it alone. At Bridgewater State University, first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students have access to dedicated support through the Career Services & Internships office, including career advising,  … By Katie Vagen Show author info Katie Vagen Director of Career Development Send Email Read more » Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist Share This: Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on Facebook Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on LinkedIn Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on X Copy Link The shift from campus life to a full-time corporate role requires more than just showing up on day one. This guide breaks down the practical steps recent graduates need to take in late summer to set themselves up for success,  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 26 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Resource Spotlight Handshake (Access to Jobs & Internships) Focus2 (Insights In Yourself & Careers) What Can I Do With This Major? (Explore Majors & Careers) Forage (Develop Skills Through Projects) LinkedIn Learning (Trainings & Resources) Parker Dewey (Apply for Micro-Internships) Big Interview (Practice Interviewing) Job & Internship Opportunities Controls Engineer TEMPLE CONTROL SYSTEMS Finance Leadership Program (FLP) White Cap Sr Supplier Quality Engineer Three Point Solutions, Inc. Associate MDR/Vigilance Specialist Three Point Solutions, Inc. Operations Planning Co-Op (Hybrid) PJM Interconnection Quality Engineer Creative Business Innovations, LLC See All Jobs Labor Market Insights In partnership with Explore occupations by career categories and pathways and use real time labor market data to power your decision making. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The information below will allow you to see career outcomes for the most recent graduating class that we have surveyed.  This data is a summary of key findings, but you can read the full reports on our CSI Reports website . 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination The first destination survey provides insights on what graduates are doing within 6 months of completing their degree.  Data is collected through a survey housed in our Handshake platform and sent via email and made available on our website prior to graduation and in the months afterwards. Top Employers This is a list of the most frequently reported employers where graduates are working after completing their degree.  This is not a full listing of all employers, just the most commonly reported.  For information on top internship sites for each class year, visit our CSI Reports site for the list of Student Internship Sites . Starting Salary The salary information below is based on self-reported data from graduates willing to provide salary data for their post-graduate employment.  This is base salary and does not include bonuses or other benefits. Employment Locations BSU graduates are working all over the United States, but contribute greatly to the Massachusetts economy with over 85% of graduates working in the commonwealth on average.  Additionally many other graduates work in the New England region. United States World Top Universities Below is a listing of the most common colleges/universities that BSU graduates are attending for their continued education.  This is not an exhaustive list. Degree Types The chart below displays the types of continuing education degrees pursued by recent graduates. Fields of Study This chart shows the variety of academic programs our graduates have enrolled in after completing their degree. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Career Resources Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on X Copy Link Every year, the Career Services & Internship Program Office invites our employer partners to conduct corporate presentations on campus and … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link What Is Forage? Explore careers. Build real-world skills. Stand out to employers. Forage is a free, self-paced online platform that … Read More FOCUS 2 Share This: Share FOCUS 2 on Facebook Share FOCUS 2 on LinkedIn Share FOCUS 2 on X Copy Link Take the Focus 2 Assessment to learn about your values, interests, personality, skills, and interests. Career advisors can discuss and … Read More Big Interview Share This: Share Big Interview on Facebook Share Big Interview on LinkedIn Share Big Interview on X Copy Link Big Interview is an online mock interview system allowing BSU students to practice and prepare for your next job interview. … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More Indeed’s Job Search Academy Share This: Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on Facebook Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on LinkedIn Share Indeed’s Job Search Academy on X Copy Link The Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University … Read More View All Resources Featured Artic