    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/make-the-most-of-a-career-fair/": {
      "title": "Make the Most of a Career Fair",
      "description": "Make the Most of a Career Fair – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Make the Most of a Career Fair Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Planning to attend a career fair?  GREAT idea! No matter your major or class year at BSU, attending a career fair gives you valuable practice interacting and networking with employers.  Ideally, your interactions with employers and organizations at the Fair will lead to future internship and full-time job opportunities. Follow the tips below and connect with a career advisor ahead of time to discuss your plan for the event. Research Companies Find the list of companies that will be attending the fair by checking the organizer’s website.  Or, in the case of BSU career fairs, check Handshake for the list of participating organizations. Then research individual companies of interest to you. Resources such as Glassdoor.com are an excellent resource to gain valuable information. In addition, Handshake’s employers page can provide additional material in your search to find a good fit for you and your career goals. Check out companies’ hiring pages to see the roles available and analyze what exactly the responsibilities of the positions are. If you possess the qualifications listed, make sure to articulate that when meeting recruiters. If lacking in certain areas, ask what skills and experiences are desired to give you the desired qualifications. Develop Questions Prepare specific questions for each company that show your knowledge about the organization. This type of directed questioning can help distinguish you from other applicants that are merely looking to gain initial information about the company’s position offerings. Your research into the company will provide the basis for your thoughtful questions. Since the recruiters have to meet hundreds of job and internship seekers, having a clear purpose and intention with your statements will help you to be remembered. Create an elevator pitch Develop a short statement, 30 seconds to 2 minutes, about who you are that sets you apart from other candidates. Mention specific details that led you to want to work for the company and how it relates to your career goals. Remember, a relationship goes both ways, and it’s important to see the connections as beneficial to each party. It is key that you practice your elevator pitch before the fair to allow yourself to become comfortable delivering it without it seeming rehearsed. Arrive prepared With a large number of companies attending a fair, your best strategy is to target a specific set of companies to maximize your time. Make sure to have enough copies of your resume as well as a pen and pad to take down important notes when speaking to company representatives. Make sure all social media profiles, such as LinkedIn, Facebook, TikTok, and Instagram are appropriately managed since recruiters will check them. Also, unless it is indicated differently on the organizer’s website, it is imperative that you dress in a business suit or appropriate work attire to showcase your professionalism when attending the fair. Follow Up Collect business cards or contact information from the recruiters that you speak to thank them for their time in a prompt manner. In addition, you can inquire about open positions that may not have been discussed during the fair. Upcoming Career Fairs Job & Internship Fair Thursday, September 17, 2026 1:00 – 3:30 PM Rondileau Student Union (RSU) Ballroom Health Professions Graduate School Fair Wednesday, October 28, 2026 1:30 – 3:30 PM Rondileau Student Union (RSU) Ballroom Summer Internship Fair Thursday, February 25, 2027 (Inclement weather date: Thursday, March 4, 2027) 1:30 – 3:30 PM Rondileau Student Union (RSU) Ballroom MEGA Job & Internship Fair Thursday, April 8, 2027 12:00 – 3:00 PM Adrian Tinsley Center (ATC) Gym Education Career Fair Wednesday, May 5, 2027 4:00 – 6:00 PM Rondileau Student Union (RSU) Ballroom Information for Students: Prepare Your Resume Using our Resume Writing Guide. Read our packet Job Fair Preparation Guide. Schedule an appointment with us to have your resume reviewed. Wear Professional Attire!  Utilize the Bear Essentials Closet for free professional clothing.  Visit RSU 104 to check it out! Suggest an Employer Information for Faculty: ​​​​​​​ Please encourage your students to attend!  We love when you bring your classes and inform your advisees.  Consider offering extra credit to those that participate.  You are welcome to attend as well, and if you have an industry contact you’d like to see at the fair, please email Tracey Gray, Associate Director of Employer Engagement & Outreach with your ideas and contacts. All faculty and staff have a Handshake student account setup for them so you can show advisees information and resources.  Your username is your full email address and corresponding password. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters Tips to Prepare for the MEGA Job & Internship Fair! Share This: Share Tips to Prepare for the MEGA Job & Internship Fair! on Facebook Share Tips to Prepare for the MEGA Job & Internship Fair! on LinkedIn Share Tips to Prepare for the MEGA Job & Internship Fair! on X Copy Link As you get ready for the Mega Job & Internship Fair on April 2, 2026 (12 PM – 3 PM, Tinsley Center Gym) , being prepared is key to making a strong impression at the job fair. Here are some important tips: … By Alyvia Nater Show author info Alyvia Nater Career Peer Advisor 