      "title": "Negotiate an Offer",
      "description": "Negotiate an Offer – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Negotiate an Offer Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Negotiate an Offer Although the majority of your time and energy during your job search and interview process is focused on getting an offer, it is a good idea to think about the your ideal work situation and the type of offer you would accept, negotiate, or decline BEFORE an offer is on the table. Having thought about your priorities and needs in advance of actually receiving an offer will allow you to ask the right questions during the latter stages of the interview process and will also make the process of accepting or declining an offer less stressful. When people hear “evaluating job offer” they usually think only about the salary. First, review the factors that you should definitely weigh no matter how attractive your salary offer may look. As you read through the list, try to evaluate how important each of the factors will be to you and your preferred lifestyle: The Organization Type and size of business Financial condition, stability, and future Location(s) Philosophy, value system, and mission Company or organization reputation The Position Typical daily routine Typical work hours; anticipated overtime Room for advancement and professional development opportunities Supervisor, co-workers, and colleagues Required and desired skills Size of department Travel Hybrid, remote or in-person Benefits Salary, signing bonus, or other compensation Relocation budget Vacation time (i.e., paid time off) Savings plan (e.g., 401K or 403B) Health benefits (e.g., medical, dental, and vision) Tuition reimbursement (for self and family) Pension or retirement plan Vesting time (i.e., when a company’s contributions fully belong to you) Commuting expenses Pre-tax options (e.g., commuting, childcare, etc.) Additional Resources: Salary.com PayScale.com CareerOneStop.org Indeed.com Glassdoor.com Remember the staff at the Career Services & Internships Office can help you navigate this process. Schedule an appointment via Handshake to connect with a career advisor. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Share This: Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on Facebook Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on LinkedIn Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on X Copy Link By Vicki Salemi, career expert at Monster.com Congrats, you crushed your summer internship! If you clicked with your colleagues and boss, enjoyed the work, and felt right at home with company culture, you may be disappointed that the internship is  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Supporting BSU Graduate Students Share This: Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on Facebook Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on LinkedIn Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on X Copy Link Most graduate students are working full-time in their field while completing academic courses in the evening.   Keeping this in mind, the Career Services & Internships office has made all of our individual career advising appointments available virtually for your convenience.  You can schedule a virtual appointment with a  … By Jill Satamraju Show author info Jill Satamraju Assi