    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/search-for-a-job-internship/": {
      "title": "Search for a Job",
      "description": "Search for a Job – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Search for a Job Labor Market Insights Featured Articles Career Resources Career Resources Jobs & Internships Labor Market Insights Alumni Connections Gain Experience Career Outcomes Featured Articles Clubs & Associations Career Videos Finding a job is a process. Job functions and timelines may vary, but the required preparation is similar across all searches. Preparation includes exploring connections between majors and careers, industry research, building your professional network, and writing application materials like a resume and cover letter. Our career advisors and resources can help you prepare and strategize your search process. Handshake is our career management database where you can access full-time professional positions, internships, career fair event information, on campus interview sign-ups and on-line resources.  All students have an account with your @student.bridgew.edu email and corresponding password. Access Handshake today to see the organizations targeting BSU candidates. The Indeed Job Search Academy is a free, virtual career development program brought to you by Indeed and Bridgewater State University to help you excel in your job search. The Academy focuses on mastering the 5 key areas of the job search so you feel confident every step of the way–because everyone deserves better work. BSU students and alumni have free access to this great resource! CareerSpring – Launching your career is a whole new journey, and you don’t have to travel it alone. We provide a one-of-a-kind Career Platform to help unlock the future potential of first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students by providing career information and resources. You can explore careers, develop skills, network and get advice as well as launch your internship or job search. Visit the website to request access today! Additionally, consider exploring opportunities through an industry-specific job board or general website. Here is a sample list of industry websites and career resources (note that we are not affiliated with these organizations): LinkedIn – Connect with industry professionals and BSU alumni, identify hidden connections Indeed.com – Search for internships, part-time, and full-time job opportunities O*Net – Review different types of occupations and possible career options Occupational Outlook Handbook – Learn more about career options in various sectors Idealist.org – Identify jobs, volunteering, and internships in the nonprofit sector SchoolSpring – Explore job opportunities in the Education sector USAJobs.gov – Find opportunities in the U.S. Federal Government APA.org/education-career/undergrad/research-opportunities – Locate psychology research opportunities Artjobs.artsearch.us – Locate arts-related internships and full-time positions Biospace.com – Explore biology-related opportunities Backstage.com – Check out acting-related gigs and positions Efinancialcareers – Gain insight into careers in finance Globaljobs.org – Search for international opportunities and careers Jobs.sciencecareers.org – Discover opportunities related to STEM Journalismjobs.com – Prepare for journalism-related careers Lawjobs.com – Find career opportunities related to law Mandy.com – Find jobs related to films and productions Mediabistro.com – Identify internships and jobs in media NSF.gov/crssprgm/reu/ – Explore undergraduate and graduate research opportunities Talent Fairy – Explore jobs and resources for students interested in writing and publishing Teamworkonline.com – Identify sports-related internships and full-time positions Topschooljobs.org – Find opportunities related to education Workforgood.org – Discover careers related to nonprofits Workinsports.com – Explore sports-related opportunities Job Search Tips and Strategies Decide on 2–3 careers/job fields to pursue Network with friends, parents, faculty, alumni, and others to let them know goals and gain advice and referrals Apply to job postings and consider temporary work via temp agencies or gig sites Attend career fairs, company presentations, professional association meetings, and conferences Broaden the scope of job search to include alternative Plans A, B, and C as part of your job search strategy Track your applications on a spreadsheet, save all of your materials including job descriptions Prepare for each interview by researching the organization and create a list of field-related questions to ask Follow up after job interviews with thank you emails or cards Research salaries/benefits and know how to negotiate when offers are made Be patient. A full-time job search takes time. Stay positive and take care of yourself throughout the process Our Job Search Guide details how to get your job search started!  We outline action steps, resources and tips that will help you make your first professional job search a success! Featured Articles CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Share This: Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on Facebook Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on X Copy Link News & Articles Launching your career is a whole new journey and you don’t have to travel it alone. At Bridgewater State University, first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students have access to dedicated support through the Career Services & Internships office, including career advising,  … By Katie Vagen Show author info Katie Vagen Director of Career Development Send Email Read more » Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist Share This: Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on Facebook Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on LinkedIn Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on X Copy Link News & Articles The shift from campus life to a full-time corporate role requires more than just showing up on day one. This guide breaks down the practical steps recent graduates need to take in late summer to set themselves up for success,  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 42 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Career Resources Internship Search Guide Share This: Share Internship Search Guide on Facebook Share Internship Search Guide on LinkedIn Share Internship Search Guide on X Copy Link View Resource Job Search Guide Share This: Share Job Search Guide on Facebook Share Job Search Guide on LinkedIn Share Job Search Guide on X Copy Link View Resource References Guide Share This: Share References Guide on Facebook Share References Guide on LinkedIn Share References Guide on X Copy Link View Resource Job Fair Preparation Guide Share This: Share Job Fair Preparation Guide on Facebook Share Job Fair Preparation Guide on LinkedIn Share Job Fair Preparation Guide on X Copy Link View Resource Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions Share This: Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on Facebook Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on LinkedIn Share Attending Company Presentations/Information Sessions on X Copy Link Every year, the Career Services & Internship Program Office invites our employer partners to conduct corporate presentations on campus and … Read More Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link The nation’s largest career management platform connecting students and alumni to career resources, recruiting events, internships, and jobs across the … Read More View All Resources Featured Articles CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? Supporting BSU Graduate Students View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
