    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/hirelocally/": {
      "title": "HireLocally",
      "description": "HireLocally – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes HireLocally Announcing the #HireLocally campaign. In support of Bridgewater State University’s mission , the Career Services & Internships Office is launching a #HireLocally campaign, with an emphasis on spotlighting employers interested in and committed to recruiting local talent. #HireLocally for students Throughout the year, the Career Services & Internships Office will cultivate a list of part-time, full-time, and internship opportunities within a 75-mile radius of Bridgewater State University. All BSU students and alumni can access this designated #HireLocally search on Handshake to explore and track available opportunities in the region. We will also proactively highlight student success stories with individuals who have secured employment at these organizations through social media channels. #HireLocally for BSU alumni and employer partners Handshake job posting system – Besides designating employer partners who offer career opportunities and commit to recruiting and retaining BSU talent on Handshake, the Career Services & Internships Office will begin offering special ribbons highlighting these employers at some of our signature events. The Career Services & Internships Office will continue cultivating interest and conducting targeted outreach to employers aligned with BSU’s academic programs who want to recruit and retain BSU talent.  The goal is strengthening our footprint and positioning BSU as the premier destination for future workforce talent. We highly encourage employers to clearly list the exact work site location as part of the job and internship posting, along with any available options for students to access the work site via public transportation. How can you help? Supporting public higher education not only helps support the local and regional economy, it is a more cost effective way to attract and recruit great workforce talent. If you have any job referrals and leads, please share them with us at careerservices@bridgew.edu. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring Share This: Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on Facebook Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on LinkedIn Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on X Copy Link September is the real new year on campus. The energy is fresh but not chaotic. Students have shaken off the chaos of move-in and the shock of their first syllabus. Career centers flip the “open” sign to full brightness. Employers  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Sidebar Featured Articles September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
