    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/job-postings-handshake/": {
      "title": "Job Postings/Handshake",
      "description": "Job Postings/Handshake – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Job Postings/Handshake Handshake If you already have a Handshake account, please add Bridgewater State University to your list of schools you work with. You will then make your job and internship listings available to us and have access to registering for career fairs and on-campus interview dates. If you are not already using Handshake, create your company and profile in Handshake . Once approved, you will be able to post your opportunities. Jobs We Do Not Post on Handshake Bridgewater State University does not post or promote the following types of opportunities: Any part-time jobs or internships that occur in private residential homes are prohibited unless the residence is legally zoned for the purpose of conducting the business. Employment/entrepreneurial opportunities with compensation packages requiring prospective employees to pay start-up fees, purchase a franchise, products, or services upfront. Opportunities based on a “pyramid” or “multi-level” type networking structure requiring/encouraging the recruitment of others who recruit others to sell products and services. Babysitting or other in-home jobs and/or internships where an employee would be working out of someone’s home or dwelling. Campus/Brand Ambassador Positions and similar roles that seek students to sell or market an organization or brand on campus are not considered full-time employment nor an academic internship.  They can be posted as a part-time job and must include an hourly wage (no payment by gift cards or merchandise). Placement Agencies/Organizations offering unspecified opportunities to teach abroad, teach abroad agencies based outside of the United States, and those that charge for their services. Placement/Training Agencies or Organizations that provide training with no definitive or guaranteed job offer. Alternatives for Posting These Roles We do not vet or endorse any particular site, but provide these as a resource. Each link will open to a new website outside of BSU: BSU Guide to In-Home Learning Opportunities PDF Document Post childcare/nanny/babysitting jobs on care.com Post general jobs on Monster.com Post hourly jobs on snagajob.com Post freelance jobs on upwork.com Post local jobs on Craigslist You can also post freelance jobs on fiverr.com Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring Share This: Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on Facebook Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on LinkedIn Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on X Copy Link September is the real new year on campus. The energy is fresh but not chaotic. Students have shaken off the chaos of move-in and the shock of their first syllabus. Career centers flip the “open” sign to full brightness. Employers  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Making a Great First Interview Impression as a Recruiter Share This: Share Making a Great First Interview Impression as a Recruiter on Facebook Share Making a Great First Interview Impression as a Recruiter on LinkedIn Share Making a Great First Interview Impression as a Recruiter on X Copy Link You’ve worked hard to source and schedule top talent for your facility. The challenging job market has made it difficult, but you’re confident you have a good selection of candidates from which to choose. As you prepare to meet potential  … By HospitalRecruiting Show author