am Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Branding Opportunities Information Table Reserve a table in a high-traffic area to inform students of the opportunities available at your organization.  Hand out swag, chat with students, and advertise your brand! Industry Insiders Participate in a variety of industry-specific events including panels, speed networking, and mini job fairs.  Share your career path with students, offer them general advice about getting started in the field, and meet potential hires. Host/Post a Virtual Event Organize a virtual event and post the link on Handshake, so BSU students can register to attend. Host a company information session, highlight your company internship programs, or share the variety of careers opportunities available within your organization. Practice Interviews on Big Interview Help our students prepare for interviews by pre-recording sample interview questions on Big Interview, our practice interview software program. RESUMEMANIA Join us in reviewing students resumes during our resume review days to ensure students are “fair ready” for our major Job & Internship Fairs. Host a Micro-Internship We’ve partnered with Parker Dewey to help you engage with BSU students through micro-internships! Identify high-potential candidates early on by offering short-term, paid projects and start building your early-career talent pipeline now. Learn more about BSU’s partnership with Parker Dewey by reading the article on Parker Dewey’s website . Collaborative University Business Experiences (CUBEs) Take your organization’s problem or question to a BSU faculty member and their class; the BSU cohort will conduct research, analyze data, and present potential solutions to you at the end of the semester.  This is a great way to establish contact with a BSU professor and get to know future graduates. Learn more about the program by visiting the CUBEs Program Employer Information website. For more information on the above branding opportunities, please contact Tracey Gray at tgray@bridgew.edu . Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring Share This: Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on Facebook Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on LinkedIn Share September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring on X Copy Link September is the real new year on campus. The energy is fresh but not chaotic. Students have shaken off the chaos of move-in and the shock of their first syllabus. Career centers flip the “open” sign to full brightness. Employers  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » What are students looking for in a potential employer? Share This: Share What are students looking for in a potential employer? on Facebook Share What are students looking for in a potential employer? on LinkedIn Share What are students looking for in a potential employer? on X Copy Link Article courtesy of Universum Communications 2020’s most valued employer attributes shows a more pragmatic side to students. In relation to last year, students are increasingly focusing on renumeration and advancement opportunities offered by an employer, especially compared to the work culture elements. For example, the number of students selecting high future earnings as important increased 4% year over  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Next page » Sidebar Featured Articles September is the make-or-break month for intern hiring What are students looking for in a potential employer? 5 predictions for 2023 hiring and recruiting trends View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
