    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/cubes/": {
      "title": "CUBEs",
      "description": "CUBEs – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes CUBEs Collaborative University Business Experiences (CUBEs) Funded by Bridgewater State University’s 2019-2020 Innovation Grant, the Collaborative University Business Experiences (CUBEs) initiative brings together a team of faculty to explore ways to reinforce career readiness through curriculum. This initiative stimulated the college-wide dialogue about how to collaborate with local businesses and organizations to conduct semester-long/short CUBEs projects. CUBEs projects will help students better prepare for their future careers. Like other high-impact practices at BSU, it encourages deep learning and problem-solving skill development for students. Through clearly mapping students’ learning outcomes with career skills expected from the real world, students gain a competitive advantage on the job market and more professional confidence. Multiple upper-level undergraduate courses are designed and delivered in an innovative way and include career and professional development orientation. Although CUBEs collaboration focuses on capstone/research projects embedded in BSU’s course design, we also welcome other opportunities to collaborate with employers, such as guest speakers, facility tours, networking events, job shadowing, and internships.  For more information, visit the CUBEs program website. Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters CUBEs Program: Find Courses That Incorporate Real World Projects Share This: Share CUBEs Program: Find Courses That Incorporate Real World Projects on Facebook Share CUBEs Program: Find Courses That Incorporate Real World Projects on LinkedIn Share CUBEs Program: Find Courses That Incorporate Real World Projects on X Copy Link In addition to the opportunity to work on projects in the real world, CUBEs courses may include guest speakers, site visits with employers and networking events. Students who have participated in CUBEs projects feel more engaged in the course and  … By Laurent Troland Show author info Laurent Troland Director of Operations Send Email Read more » Sidebar Featured Articles CUBEs Program: Find Courses That Incorporate Real World Projects View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
    },
    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/channels/industry-mentors/": {
      "title": "Industry Mentors Program",
      "description": "Industry Mentors Program – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Industry Mentors Program Interested in helping future generations of BSU students explore careers in your field? Willing to share advice on how students can launch a career in your industry sector? Consider being part of the Industry Mentors program. Industry Mentors Program FAQs What is the Industry Mentors Program? The Industry Mentors program connects BSU students with BSU alumni and industry professionals in their fields of interest. Students will work closely with Career & Life Design Advisors at BSU’s Career Services & Internships Office to explore their skills, interests, personalities, and values. As they continue their self-discovery journey, the advisor will refer students to you for a career conversation (i.e., Informational Interviews) to learn more about your career experience, industry insights, and tips on launching their career in your field. How often do I meet with students? Since students will access your information through direct referrals from the Career Services & Internships Office, we only expect that you chat with students on a 1:1 basis for a 30 to 40-minute timeslot. Once the Career & Life Design Advisor makes the referral, you only need to provide us with your availability to connect with students. We will help coordinate the date and time that works for you and the student. You are not obligated to meet with the student more than once, and each semester, you will only get a maximum of five students. Are these meetings online or in person? To protect all parties involved throughout the process, we ask that the meeting be conducted virtually via Zoom or MS Teams. If you share your availability with our team members, our Career & Life Design Advisors will help coordinate the scheduling process. Do I need to prepare for these virtual meetings? What topics should I cover during these sessions? Our Career & Life Design Advisors will share a student’s resume with you during scheduling. Think of this as an informational interview or virtual coffee chat. The goal of this meeting is for students to ask you questions regarding your background, how you landed opportunities in your professional career, tips and advice on how students can learn more about your field, and training or experiences that can help students be competitive in their job or internship application process. After the session, we ask you to share general information regarding your interaction with the student with our staff. What if I can no longer commit to this program at any point during the semester? We understand things may change, and your personal and professional lives can impact your availability. All you need to do is inform our staff of your status. How can I get started? We are looking for individuals representing industries that interest BSU students. If you would like to participate in this program, please contact Dr. Gerald Tang, Executive Director of Career Services & Internships, at c2tang@bridgew.edu . We will schedule a brief call to learn more about your interests and background and share additional information. Industry Mentor Profiles Kathy Baldwin – The Arc of Plymouth and Upper Cape Cod Kathy Baldwin is a nonprofit executive and Licensed Independent Clinical Social Worker with more than 25 years of experience across social service organizations. She currently serves as Vice President of Community Engagement and Advancement at The Arc of Plymouth and Upper Cape Cod, where she leads donor stewardship, grant development, communications, community partnerships, and initiatives aligned with the organization’s strategic plan. Kathy’s career has centered on strengthening mission-driven organizations and creating meaningful opportunities for people with disabilities, children, families, and communities. Her early professional experience in child welfare, therapeutic foster care, and children’s behavioral health helped shape her person-centered approach and deep commitment to listening, collaboration, and practical problem-solving. Across progressive leadership roles at The Arc, she has guided quality improvement, risk management, licensing and accreditation readiness, staff training, policy development, legislative advocacy, service expansion, and cross-functional strategic initiatives. Her work has included leading successful national accreditation review processes, supporting the development of new residential and community-based services, securing state contracts and grant funding, and building meaningful partnerships with funders, legislators, provider coalitions, families, and self-advocates. In addition to her nonprofit leadership experience, Kathy serves as a federal grant peer reviewer for the Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration. She has also enjoyed mentoring emerging social work professionals as a field instructor for Simmons University and Bridgewater State University. As an Industry Mentor, Kathy welcomes conversations with students who are exploring careers in nonprofit leadership, social work, disability services, child and family services, advocacy, fundraising, grant writing, program development and operations, and community engagement. She looks forward to connecting with students as they explore their own paths and is excited to share insights from her own professional journey. Kathy earned a Bachelor of Arts from Villanova University and a Master of Social Service from Bryn Mawr College. Shaped by formative service experiences with AmeriCorps and the Jesuit Volunteer Corps, she remains active in the community through the Rotary Club of Plymouth and a local Human Rights Committee. Carlyn Mason, Class of 2020 – Granite Telecom Hi everyone! I’m Carlyn Mason, a 2020 graduate of BSU. My career journey has taken me from the classroom to the corporate world, and I’m a firm believer in hard work, loyalty, and problem-solving—skills I’d love to share with you. For years, I loved working with children as a babysitter, camp counselor, and eventually a first-grade teacher. In 2023, I made a big leap into corporate training – nerve-wracking but exciting change. Just two years later, I’m now leading the Sales Onboarding program at Granite Telecom. I know how daunting it can be to figure out your path after college. That’s why I’d be honored to assist and mentor BSU students. It’s okay to try something and change your mind; there’s plenty of time to explore different roles and find your fit. I’m an open book when it comes to mentoring, and there’s no such thing as a “silly” question. Whether you need help with a specific skill, prepping for an interview, or just have questions about work life after college, I’m here to help in any way I can. Cortney Toomey – Enterprise Mobility As an HR professional at Enterprise Mobility, I have over three years of experience supporting employees and leaders across multiple states in areas such as talent development, training, onboarding, recruiting, and employee support. I enjoy helping individuals identify their strengths and opportunities, grow their careers, and reach their goals. I earned a Bachelor of Science from Bridgewater State University in Human Resource Management with a minor in Graphic Design. Outside of work, I live in Nashua, New Hampshire, with my fiancé and our corgi, Rex, and strongly believe in the value of lifelong learning. I am so excited to be a part of this program and look forward to partnering with students and learning about their career goals! Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters How to Grow Your Network Without Awkward Small Talk Share This: Share How to Grow Your Network Without Awkward Small Talk on Facebook Share How to Grow Your Network Without Awkward Small Talk on LinkedIn Share How to Grow Your Network Without Awkward Small Talk on X Copy Link Stepping into a new field comes with a unique set of challenges – one of the biggest being the need to build a strong professional network. For those who thrive in structured conversations and prefer more profound, more meaningful discussions  … By Ivy Exec Show author info Ivy Exec is your dedicated career development resource. facebook instagram linkedin twitter Read more » Sidebar Featured Articles How to Grow Your Network Without Awkward Small Talk View All Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
