    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/support-bsu-works/": {
      "title": "Support #BSU Works – Career Services &  Internship Program",
      "description": "Support #BSU Works – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes At Bridgewater State University’s Career Services & Internships Office, we believe every BSU student should have access to industry-leading career development resources and be equipped with career and life design tools, a professional network, and experiences to become career-ready for the ever-changing workforce. Your support is needed to help us make this happen! Support us through donation: Funding for Unpaid Internships – BSU offers multiple funding opportunities to help students advance their careers and financially support their internship pursuits throughout the year. Your contribution helps propel students to pursue valuable internship experiences and ultimately land amazing opportunities. Career Services for Greater Needs – BSU’s Career Services & Internships Office establish this fund to support students to pursue professional development opportunities such as participating in professional association activities and conferences, attending industry-specific trainings, funding students for graduate school entrance exams, and helping the office to add industry-leading career resources. Donate to the Internship Fund (Select Internships under the drop down) Donate to the Career Services for Greater Needs (Select Other and Enter Career Services for Greater Needs) BSU alumni and employers play a vital role in paving the way for future generations of students to access valuable professional networks and to recruit students to join your organization. Alumni and employers can participate in some of the following activities: Attend Job & Internship Fairs to represent your organization and recruit students for internships and jobs Serve on career panels and share insight with current students Post jobs and internships on Handshake Serve as a volunteer industry coaches by connecting with students through one-on-one sessions virtually Serve as alumni mentor for current students or recent graduates Host a group of students at your organization for career exploration through our employer site visit program, BearTREK Ready to join this movement? Email us at careerservices@bridgew.edu. Go Bears! Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
    },
    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/csi-reports/": {
      "title": "CSI Reports",
      "description": "CSI Reports – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes CSI Reports Career Learning Outcomes At BSU, we believe all students deserve to have the necessary career education, professional network, practical experiences, and life design plans to navigate their career endeavors . At the end of their academic journey, BSU students will have had the opportunity to: Establish and utilize a professional network  to become an engaged citizen Create and implement career and life design plans Participate in experiential learning and high-impact practices Develop and articulate industry-relevant skills Build lifelong professional skills to manage their careers Career Services & Internships Strategic Plan: 2024-2028 The Career Services & Internships (CSI) Office has identified four main goals in this strategic plan: Goal 1: Infuse career education and life design into the fabric of the university as part of the BSUWorks initiative. Aligned with University’s Strategic Plan 2.0 goals: 1F6, 2B5, 2D Goal 2: Center equity-minded practices in our work. Aligned with University’s Strategic Plan 2.0 goals: 1A4, 1A6 Goal 3: Amplify BSU’s workforce and economic impact by positioning BSU as the engine and supplier of local workforce talent. Aligned with University’s Strategic Plan 2.0 goals: 1F6, 4A, 4B, 4C, 4D Goal 4: Prioritize organizational effectiveness, acquire and utilize industry-leading resources and technology, and emphasize staff’s professional development and well-being. Aligned with University’s Strategic Plan 2.0 goals: 1C3, 2E, 3B2, 3C C heck out the full document of the CSI 2024-2028 Strategic Plan Career Services & Internships Strategic Plan: 2024-2028 CSI 2024-2028 Strategic Plan (2) Download Career Services & Internships Annual Impact Reports Career Services & Internships Impact Report 2024-2025 Want to learn more about our work? Check out our 2024-2025 Impact Report: https://simplebooklet.com/bsucsiannualreport#page=1 CSI 24-25 Impact Report Download Career Services & Internships Impact Report 2023-2024 Want to learn more about our work? Check out our 2023-2024 Annual Report: CSI 2023-2024 Annual Report Download Career Services & Internships First Destination Survey Reports Class of 2024 First Destination Survey First Destination Survey Class of 2024 Download Class of 2023 First Destination Survey First Destination Survey Class of 2023 Download Career Services & Internships Data Dashboards Student Internship Sites: Fall 2023 – Summer 2025 Class of 2024 Alumni Location of Employment View details on where our Class of 2024 alumni are working within 6 months of graduation: https://public.tableau.com/views/FDS24Workbook2/FDSFY24EmployedData?:language=en-US&:sid=&:redirect=auth&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link Student Internship Sites Class of 2025 Internships Sites FDS Class of 2025 Download Class of 2024 Class of 2024 Internship Sites Download Class of 2023 Internship Sites for Website Class of 2023 Download Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm F Friday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Bridgewater State University"
