    "https://careers.bridgew.edu/blog/": {
      "title": "Blog – Career Services &  Internship Program",
      "description": "Blog – Career Services &  Internship Program | Bridgewater State University BSU and Career Services & Internships will be closed on Monday, September 7th for the Labor Day holiday. New: AI Search is live — ask any career question and get instant answers from our resources. Just click on the \"U\" message icon in the bottom right corner. Log in for personalized results. Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Schedule an Appointment Request a Workshop Customize Your Experience Who You Are Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Non-Degree Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Prospective Students & Guests Affinities/Identities Asian, Pacific Islanders, & Native American Black/African American First-Generation International Students Latine LGBTQIA+ Students With Disabilities Undocumented Students Veterans Women Career Interests Aviation Business, Accounting and Finance Communications, Marketing and Media Counseling & Human Services Education Fine & Performing Arts Health Care and Wellness Public Administration, Government, and Law STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics) Technology and Cybersecurity Undeclared Students/Explore Career Options Career Resources Bear Essentials Career Readiness: What Employers Are Looking For Cooperative Education (Co-op) Program Create a Resume or Cover Letter Digital Content Library Expand Your Network Explore Your Interests / Self Assessment Find an Internship Internship Funding Make the Most of a Career Fair Negotiate an Offer Prepare for an Interview Prepare for Graduate School Professional Development Funding Search for a Job Signature Internship Programs Design Your Career at BSU Recruit BSU Talent Employer Services HireLocally Job Postings/Handshake Career Fairs & Events Branding Opportunities Internship Information for Employers Internship FAQs CUBEs Industry Mentors Program Recruiting Policies Support #BSU Works About Us Mission & Memberships CSI Reports Staff Location, Parking and Social Media Schedule Appointments Vendor/Resource Requests Career Outcomes Search all Posts Search Skip filter options to posts Latest News Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness Share This: Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on Facebook Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on LinkedIn Share One Goal for This Semester: Build Your Career Readiness on X Copy Link With the new semester underway, comes new experiences, and new opportunities to learn, grow, and prepare for your future. Whether you’re just beginning your first year at BSU or set to graduate this semester, developing your career readiness is an  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students Share This: Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on Facebook Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on LinkedIn Share CareerSpring: A Resource that Expands Support for First-Generation Students on X Copy Link Launching your career is a whole new journey and you don’t have to travel it alone. At Bridgewater State University, first-generation and/or low-income (FGLI) students have access to dedicated support through the Career Services & Internships office, including career advising,  … By Katie Vagen Show author info Katie Vagen Director of Career Development Send Email Read more » Finding the Right Major for You Share This: Share Finding the Right Major for You on Facebook Share Finding the Right Major for You on LinkedIn Share Finding the Right Major for You on X Copy Link If you’re still deciding on a major or wanting to make a change, you’re not alone. According to a the National Academic Advising Association (NACADA) “up to 75% of college students change their major at least once” during their educational  … By Anastasia Krueger Show author info Anastasia Krueger Early Career Engagement Advisor Send Email Read more » Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist Share This: Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on Facebook Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on LinkedIn Share Transitioning from College to Corporate: Your Late-Summer Prep Checklist on X Copy Link The shift from campus life to a full-time corporate role requires more than just showing up on day one. This guide breaks down the practical steps recent graduates need to take in late summer to set themselves up for success,  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Share This: Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on Facebook Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on LinkedIn Share How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer on X Copy Link By Vicki Salemi, career expert at Monster.com Congrats, you crushed your summer internship! If you clicked with your colleagues and boss, enjoyed the work, and felt right at home with company culture, you may be disappointed that the internship is  … By College Recruiter Show author info College Recruiter believes that every student and recent grad deserves a great career. facebook linkedin youtube Read more » What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? Share This: Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on Facebook Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on LinkedIn Share What Is a Staffing Firm or a Temporary Employment Agency? on X Copy Link A staffing firm acts as a bridge between employers and job seekers. Companies rely on staffing agencies to find qualified employees quickly, while job seekers gain access to opportunities that may not be advertised publicly. Many staffing firms recruit for  … By Gerald Tang Show author info Gerald Tang Executive Director Send Email Read more » Faculty Are Key to Student Career Success Share This: Share Faculty Are Key to Student Career Success on Facebook Share Faculty Are Key to Student Career Success on LinkedIn Share Faculty Are Key to Student Career Success on X Copy Link Faculty have the most direct and regular contact with our students and thus play a pivotal role in their career success. Through coursework, advising, research and other experiential activities, students learn and gain invaluable skills. The one issue is students  … By Laurent Troland Show author info Laurent Troland Director of Operations Send Email Read more » Supporting BSU Graduate Students Share This: Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on Facebook Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on LinkedIn Share Supporting BSU Graduate Students on X Copy Link Most graduate students are working full-time in their field while completing academic courses in the evening.   Keeping this in mind, the Career Services & Internships office has made all of our individual career advising appointments available virtually for your convenience.  You can schedule a virtual appointment with a  … By Jill Satamraju Show author info Jill Satamraju Assistant Director of Internships & Career Development Send Email Read more » Why Starting Early is Essential for a Career in Public Administration, Government, or Law Share This: Share Why Starting Early is Essential for a Career in Public Administration, Government, or Law on Facebook Share Why Starting Early is Essential for a Career in Public Administration, Government, or Law on LinkedIn Share Why Starting Early is Essential for a Career in Public Administration, Government, or Law on X Copy Link Many students begin college thinking that if they just work hard and earn good grades, their career path will naturally unfold on its own.  The reality is that while your academic preparation is critical, there is more you need to consider – especially when  … By Heather Connell Show author info Heather Connell Career & Life Design Advisor Send Email Read more » Nora Sperling ’26’s Journey to Meaningful Work at BIDMC Share This: Share Nora Sperling ’26’s Journey to Meaningful Work at BIDMC on Facebook Share Nora Sperling ’26’s Journey to Meaningful Work at BIDMC on LinkedIn Share Nora Sperling ’26’s Journey to Meaningful Work at BIDMC on X Copy Link Finding a career that aligns with both your skills, and your values can be incredibly rewarding. For one Bridgewater State University alumna, a degree in Communications, hands-on internship experience, and a passion for giving back led her to a career in  … By Katie Muldoon Show author info Katie Muldoon Marketing and Program Coordinator Send Email Read more » Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 22 Next page » Sidebar Follow Here For More Career Content! Job & Internship Opportunities Political Canvasser North Shore Strategies Hudson Institute Political Studies Summer Fellowship in Theory and Practice of Politics Hudson Institute Business Development Executive Metric Search Manufacturing Technical Writer (6 months) Quest Global Account Manager Integrated Services Data Axle See All Jobs Contact & Location Phone 508-531-1328 Email careerservices@bridgew.edu Website https://careers.bridgew.edu/ Address Rondileau Student Union (RSU), Room 104 19 Park Avenue Bridgewater, MA 02325 Office Hours M Monday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm T Tuesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm W Wednesday 9:00 am - 5:00 pm TH Thursday 9: